57
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:04,710
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: to answer questions on the proposed budget of the Office of the President.

58
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:14,280
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: To sponsor the proposed budget of the Office of the President, the Senior Vice Chair of the Committee on Appropriations, the Hon. Abet Garcia of the 2nd District of Bataan, is hereby recognized.

59
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:22,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Thank you very much, Madam Speaker, Majority Floor Leader, Distinguished Guests and Colleagues. Magandang umaga po sa ating lahat.

60
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:34,300
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: On behalf of the Committee on Appropriations, I have the honor to sponsor the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget of the Office of the President.

61
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:49,080
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The Office of the President is the apex of the executive branch, the office from which the President as Chief Executive and Commander-in-Chief directs the entire government.

62
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:52,920
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: What we appropriate for it?

63
00:23:52,940 --> 00:23:58,420
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: We appropriate for the working of the presidency itself.

64
00:23:58,420 --> 00:24:22,200
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The 2027 budget, the office proposes a 10,155,758,000 or 10.16 billion inclusive of the retirement and life insurance premium.

65
00:24:22,940 --> 00:24:36,600
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: That is about 0.14% of the 7.2 trillion national budget, roughly one-seventh of 1%.

66
00:24:36,600 --> 00:24:43,820
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: For the highest office of the land, this is a lean proposal, Madam Speaker.

67
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:46,740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Its shape is simple.

68
00:24:46,740 --> 00:24:50,100
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: By allotment class, it is an operating budget.

69
00:24:51,620 --> 00:24:52,740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Maintenance and other operations.

70
00:24:52,940 --> 00:24:59,240
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Operating expense account for 7.46 billion or 74%.

71
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:05,320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Personal services comprise of 1.86 billion or 18%.

72
00:25:05,320 --> 00:25:13,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Capital outlay stands at 839.66 million or a mere 8%.

73
00:25:13,940 --> 00:25:21,220
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: By source, it is almost entirely new appropriations at 99.29%.

74
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:22,320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Placed squarely.

75
00:25:22,940 --> 00:25:26,740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Before this chamber for scrutiny.

76
00:25:28,100 --> 00:25:29,920
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: What does it fund?

77
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:31,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Two pillars, Madam Speaker.

78
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:42,740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: General administration and support at 2.74 billion and operations at 7.41 billion delivered through four programs.

79
00:25:43,520 --> 00:25:49,560
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The largest is the Presidential Oversight Program at 5.37 billion.

80
00:25:49,560 --> 00:25:52,920
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: It covers directives and clearances.

81
00:25:52,940 --> 00:25:55,980
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Policy on national interventions.

82
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:58,860
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Oversight of national security.

83
00:25:59,700 --> 00:26:04,880
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Public assistance and performance monitoring across the executive.

84
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:09,860
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Next is the Executive Staff Service at 1.63 billion.

85
00:26:10,460 --> 00:26:14,160
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Covering the President's missions and state visits.

86
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:19,320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Security, official events and documents.

87
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:22,320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The Advisory Program at 184.6 million

88
00:26:22,940 --> 00:26:29,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and the Legal and Legislative Services Program at 180 million.

89
00:26:29,940 --> 00:26:31,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Complete operations.

90
00:26:31,940 --> 00:26:37,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The latter funds the review of the very bills we pass.

91
00:26:37,940 --> 00:26:41,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And the office binds itself to account for every peso.

92
00:26:41,940 --> 00:26:52,700
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Under its special provision, it must file quarterly reports on its financial and physical accomplishments within 30 days of each quarter.

93
00:26:52,940 --> 00:27:01,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Post them online and notify both houses and their committees on appropriations and finance.

94
00:27:01,940 --> 00:27:09,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Transparency here is not a promise, it is a condition of the appropriation.

95
00:27:11,940 --> 00:27:22,230
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Now to what my colleagues will notice at once and what I present with pride, not apology, on a comparable basis.

96
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:24,270
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Net of retirement

97
00:27:24,280 --> 00:27:26,200
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and life insurance premium

98
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,870
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and pension,

99
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:33,790
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The office's budget falls from 28.03 billion to 10.08 billion.

100
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:41,240
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And that is a reduction of 17.95 billion, or 64.02%.

101
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:46,140
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The Office of the President is asking for

102
00:27:46,440 --> 00:27:49,440
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: marked less.

103
00:27:49,440 --> 00:27:50,440
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And that's a reason.

104
00:27:50,440 --> 00:28:08,240
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The reason is plain. Some P17.55 billion of that drop is the completion of the locally funded projects in 2026 budget, principally our hosting of the ASEAN 2026.

105
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:29,540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: That duty is successfully done. Not a single peso of it is carried in the 2027 budget. And even setting ASEAN aside, the regular programs were trimmed by a further 392.52 million or 3.75%.

106
00:28:29,540 --> 00:28:38,040
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: This is an office that tightened its own belt before asking our people or any agency.

107
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:56,280
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker, this is a budget that funds the presidency at a fraction of the national total, carried an unchanged workforce, bound to quarterly transparency, and smaller than the year before.

108
00:28:56,700 --> 00:29:07,480
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: I stand ready, together with the resource person headed by our Executive Secretary, Ralph Recto, to answer any questions in this chamber.

109
00:29:08,020 --> 00:29:08,220
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: We thank you.

110
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:18,580
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: With that, I respectfully sponsor and commend the fiscal year 2027 budget of the Office of the President and move for its favorable consideration.

111
00:29:19,620 --> 00:29:23,200
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker, maraming salamat at magandang umaga po sa ating lahat.

112
00:29:24,100 --> 00:29:24,920
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

113
00:29:25,480 --> 00:29:30,760
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Madam Speaker, I move to recognize the Honorable Rene Co. of the Kabataan Party List to interpolate the sponsor.

114
00:29:31,260 --> 00:29:33,380
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Rene Co. is hereby recognized.

115
00:29:33,380 --> 00:29:38,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Speaker. At magandang umaga po.

116
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:39,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: The distinguished sponsor natin.

117
00:29:40,060 --> 00:29:44,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Will the distinguished sponsor yield to a few questions in relation to the budget of the Office of the President?

118
00:29:44,900 --> 00:29:47,300
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yes, Madam Speaker. At magandang umaga po.

119
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:55,300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, ang ating mga katanungan dito ay mga natanong na rin natin over the course of the budget cycle.

120
00:29:55,740 --> 00:30:00,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ngunit sa mga paglalatag ng mga...

121
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: mandato, the Office of the President would be in the best position to answer these questions.

122
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:12,780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang una nating tanong ay patungkol po sa Barangay Development Program to support the

123
00:30:12,780 --> 00:30:17,480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: activities of the National Task Force to End Local Communist Armed Conflict or NTF-ELCAC.

124
00:30:18,100 --> 00:30:21,680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Bilang chairman ng NTF-ELCAC ang Pangulo.

125
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:28,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Alam ba ng Pangulo kung ano ang proseso ng pagpapaklear ng mga barangay para maging

126
00:30:28,020 --> 00:30:30,900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: eligible beneficiaries ng Barangay Development Program?

127
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:34,060
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yes, Madam Speaker.

128
00:30:34,980 --> 00:30:40,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Maari po bang madetali, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor, yung proseso na ito?

129
00:30:40,860 --> 00:30:48,360
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Well, one of the major process, Madam Speaker, ito po'y dumadaan sa mga local peace and

130
00:30:48,360 --> 00:30:55,780
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: development councils from the LGU up to the region at umakit po ito sa National Peace

131
00:30:55,780 --> 00:30:58,000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and Order Council.

132
00:30:58,020 --> 00:31:05,480
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And ito po ang nagde-declare ng insurgency-free sa ating mga localities.

133
00:31:06,100 --> 00:31:13,660
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And kapag ito po'y nadeclare na insurgency-free, they would be eligible for the fund under

134
00:31:13,660 --> 00:31:18,280
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: the LGSF or yung Barangay Development Program, Madam Speaker.

135
00:31:19,220 --> 00:31:22,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, tinanong po kasi natin sa DILG.

136
00:31:22,860 --> 00:31:27,060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Bilang sila po yung nagkukulit ng listahan.

137
00:31:27,300 --> 00:31:27,960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Tinanong rin po.

138
00:31:28,020 --> 00:31:29,020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At tinanong natin sa DBM.

139
00:31:29,460 --> 00:31:36,260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Bilang sila po yung tumatanggap ng listahan at later sila ang magbibigay ng pondo or

140
00:31:36,260 --> 00:31:43,980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: mag-aalat ng pondo sa NEP para mabigay ng grant yung nasa loob ng program.

141
00:31:44,560 --> 00:31:51,520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ang sabi po nila, Barangays undergo community support programs and retooled community support

142
00:31:51,520 --> 00:31:53,960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: programs led by DILG.

143
00:31:53,960 --> 00:31:57,960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: At ang listahan, pagka natapos na...

144
00:31:58,020 --> 00:32:04,080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Pagka natapos na yung sumisyon na ito, ay i-e-endorso ng NTF-LCAC to DBM.

145
00:32:04,520 --> 00:32:09,640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So ang tanong natin, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, ito lang ba ang requirement para maging eligible?

146
00:32:10,160 --> 00:32:18,100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Automatically, in-e-endorse lang din ba ng NTF-LCAC kung ano mang mga listahan yung makarating sa kanila?

147
00:32:18,640 --> 00:32:25,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ano pong mga iba't-ibang proseso para ma-verify na kung ano man po yung nakalagay sa listahan,

148
00:32:25,940 --> 00:32:27,940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: kung ano pong activity yung nangyayari?

149
00:32:28,020 --> 00:32:34,360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa mga local peace councils ay naisagawa po. Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

150
00:32:37,860 --> 00:32:40,740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Sa mga local development... Sorry.

151
00:32:41,040 --> 00:32:45,740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Sa mga local peace and order council, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleagues,

152
00:32:46,100 --> 00:32:51,260
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: kasama po dito ang armed forces, PNP, and other agencies,

153
00:32:51,260 --> 00:32:57,260
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and they validate in context itong mga insurgency clearance.

154
00:32:58,020 --> 00:32:59,580
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: They're LGUs.

155
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:07,920
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Bukod po dyan, yung ating mga peace and order councils is chaired by the mayors, the governors,

156
00:33:08,620 --> 00:33:10,560
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: kaya ito po'y may konteksto.

157
00:33:11,140 --> 00:33:20,420
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And once, together with the armed forces, these localities are validated as insurgency-free,

158
00:33:20,420 --> 00:33:27,780
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: they will be eligible for the Barangay Development Program assistance, Madam Speaker.

159
00:33:28,020 --> 00:33:34,020
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, from the ground up po ito, at kapag na-validate po ito from the ground up,

160
00:33:34,280 --> 00:33:42,980
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: dun pa lang po umaakyat sa ating NDFL-CAC, and they refer this to DBM and DILG

161
00:33:42,980 --> 00:33:47,600
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: para po maging eligible dito po sa Barangay Development Program Fund.

162
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:52,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor. Ano pong ibig sabihin ng in context, validated in context?

163
00:33:52,860 --> 00:33:57,860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Maari po bang makapaglatag ng isang senaryo na nasabi ng AFD?

164
00:33:58,020 --> 00:34:05,380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: PNP, PNP, other agencies do that kind of validation habang, ano po, pag ginagawa po yung activity?

165
00:34:05,900 --> 00:34:07,180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

166
00:34:07,620 --> 00:34:13,520
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yeah. What I mean, Madam Speaker, na in context, kasi it's very hard for the national government

167
00:34:13,520 --> 00:34:20,000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: or the national level to validate yung pagiging insurgency-free ng isang lugar

168
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:23,400
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: from the macro level or the national level.

169
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:27,060
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, the people on the ground know the situation best.

170
00:34:28,020 --> 00:34:33,220
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And these are the local government officials, the mayors, the barangay officials,

171
00:34:34,040 --> 00:34:38,620
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: together with the national agencies in that locality.

172
00:34:39,380 --> 00:34:44,540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yan po ang ibig sabihin kong in context, and they would know more the situation on the ground.

173
00:34:44,940 --> 00:34:49,600
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And when they refer this, and after validation from the region and the national,

