Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Executive secretary.

1104
01:38:26,960 --> 01:38:29,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Executive secretary, malaki rin.

1105
01:38:30,900 --> 01:38:34,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 500 million for a multipurpose building, no?

1106
01:38:35,260 --> 01:38:47,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Samantala, all the vast majority of LGSF, particular FALGU recipients, natatanggap nila 30 million and below.

1107
01:38:48,380 --> 01:38:50,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, yun ang question natin.

1108
01:38:51,400 --> 01:38:53,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano ba ang kriteriya nito and who decides?

1109
01:38:53,840 --> 01:38:55,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That's why we say this is highly discretionary.

1110
01:38:56,960 --> 01:39:00,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I also don't believe in presidential pork.

1111
01:39:00,720 --> 01:39:05,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung sinong malapit sa kusina, eka nga, yun ang makakatanggap ng malaki.

1112
01:39:05,020 --> 01:39:06,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun po.

1113
01:39:06,520 --> 01:39:22,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon, ano po ang papel ng Office of the President sa pag-decide kung sino ang makakatanggap at magkano sa mga LGU para dito sa LGSF na ito.

1114
01:39:22,520 --> 01:39:26,200
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleagues.

1115
01:39:26,200 --> 01:39:39,380
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: First of all, ito pong LGSF is part of the General Appropriations Act which we passed as being having the power of the purse.

1116
01:39:39,380 --> 01:39:50,500
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, ine-execute lang ito ng executive headed by our president ang pag-distribute nito according to the guidelines.

1117
01:39:51,200 --> 01:39:56,180
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: This is implemented by the DBM pero demand-driven po ito.

1118
01:39:56,200 --> 01:40:10,900
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: May portal at dun po nag-a-apply yung iba't ibang LGU all around the country para humingi po o mag-request ng assistance sa local government support fund.

1119
01:40:11,480 --> 01:40:21,800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And also, this is supported by jurisprudence ng mga Supreme Court decision na constitutional, sinasabing constitutional, ang local government support fund.

1120
01:40:21,800 --> 01:40:25,800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, the executive is merely implementing the...

1121
01:40:26,200 --> 01:40:31,620
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: ...budget which was passed by both houses of Congress.

1122
01:40:32,580 --> 01:40:33,960
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker, distinguish fully.

1123
01:40:34,580 --> 01:40:35,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, merely implementing.

1124
01:40:36,920 --> 01:40:38,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: But let me also...

1125
01:40:39,400 --> 01:40:49,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In implementing, kailangan pa rin pong sundin ng Office of the President ang batas.

1126
01:40:49,540 --> 01:40:51,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ano po ang umiiral na batas?

1127
01:40:52,500 --> 01:40:55,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sinasabi po sa administrative...

1128
01:40:56,200 --> 01:41:22,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ...administrative code, let me read, that this is section 6, book 5, section 35, I hope I remember that correctly, of the administrative code on special budgets for lump sum appropriations.

1129
01:41:22,140 --> 01:41:26,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, this applies to all lump sum appropriations including...

1130
01:41:26,200 --> 01:41:27,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ...the LGSF.

1131
01:41:28,080 --> 01:41:32,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, sorry, chapter 5, section 35 of the administrative code.

1132
01:41:33,180 --> 01:41:34,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What does it say?

1133
01:41:34,980 --> 01:41:52,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Expenditures from lump sum appropriations authorized for any purpose or for any department, office, or agency in any annual general appropriations act or other act and from any fund of the national government shall be made in accordance with the special budget to be approved by the President.

1134
01:41:52,500 --> 01:41:54,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, napakalinaw po.

1135
01:41:54,960 --> 01:41:56,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: To be approved by the President.

1136
01:41:56,200 --> 01:42:04,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, yung mga releases po sa LGSF, is it in accordance with section 35, approved by the President?

1137
01:42:05,480 --> 01:42:06,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes or no lang po?

1138
01:42:26,200 --> 01:42:54,400
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleagues, the executive is implementing the LGSF the way the legislative approved it through the general appropriations act.

1139
01:42:54,400 --> 01:42:54,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

1140
01:42:54,540 --> 01:42:56,180
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, that is the legal basis.

1141
01:42:56,200 --> 01:43:12,260
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The legal basis for the LGSF followed by the DBM circular, which they passed, medyo makapal nga yun, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleagues, with regards to the implementation of the local government support fund.

1142
01:43:12,280 --> 01:43:14,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, let me just, so I take that as a no.

1143
01:43:14,460 --> 01:43:19,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po sinusunod itong section 35, kundi daw yung GAA.

1144
01:43:19,740 --> 01:43:26,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Let me just note that nowhere in the GAA does it explicitly repeal or amend.

1145
01:43:26,200 --> 01:43:40,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, in other words, hindi pwedeng ma-circumvent yung presidential approval, which, let me note, kaya nandyan yan, is precisely it is a safeguard against abuse of lump sum funds.

1146
01:43:41,620 --> 01:43:49,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya po nagre-require ng approval ng Presidente, eh dahil kayo po ang magche-check kung walang abuso dito.

1147
01:43:50,280 --> 01:43:55,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, okay, noted po na mukhang hindi nyo sinusunod ang section 35.

1148
01:43:55,580 --> 01:43:56,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

1149
01:43:56,200 --> 01:43:58,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Let me move on, dahil paubos na ang ating oras.

1150
01:43:59,740 --> 01:44:00,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Flood control.

1151
01:44:01,360 --> 01:44:14,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In this very hall, alam natin, 2025 zona, nagsabi ang Pangulo, mahiya naman kayo, at dyan na nagsimula yung investigasyon sa flood control corruption.

1152
01:44:15,160 --> 01:44:15,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

1153
01:44:18,220 --> 01:44:26,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The cabinet members have been promoting the line, notably Secretary Vince Dizon.

1154
01:44:26,200 --> 01:44:40,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa kanyang mga interview, sabi niya, according to news reports, si dating House Speaker na ang tinutukoy na biggest fish sa ngayon, ayon kay DPWH Secretary Vince Dizon.

1155
01:44:40,780 --> 01:44:42,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, yun ang linya ngayon ng palasyo.

1156
01:44:43,280 --> 01:44:44,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ayan na, meron na tayong nakulog.

1157
01:44:44,780 --> 01:44:47,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The biggest fish is already arrested.

1158
01:44:49,060 --> 01:44:49,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

1159
01:44:50,120 --> 01:44:55,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi naman ni Senator Lacson, Marcos' critics should be silent.

1160
01:44:55,200 --> 01:44:55,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

1161
01:44:56,200 --> 01:44:58,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: After the arrest of the former speaker.

1162
01:44:59,740 --> 01:44:59,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So,

1163
01:44:59,840 --> 01:45:00,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So,

1164
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:08,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Parang ang script, ayan na ang biggest fish, tigil na natin, tapos na, we can move on, nandyan na yung biggest fish.

1165
01:45:08,920 --> 01:45:13,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero nandyan na nga ba? What about the President himself?

1166
01:45:15,180 --> 01:45:16,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Why do I say this?

1167
01:45:16,580 --> 01:45:24,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Let me quote an important speech made by Senator Lacson.

1168
01:45:25,600 --> 01:45:28,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At the time he was still chair of the Blue Ribbon Committee, Senate.

1169
01:45:28,560 --> 01:45:31,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Transcript, November 17, 2025.

1170
01:45:32,880 --> 01:45:33,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Let me quote.

1171
01:45:58,560 --> 01:46:09,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Now, Yusek Trigiv-Olaivar, other personalities, anyway, regarding the 100 billion, being raked down kasi, ni-review niya yung kanyang notes.

1172
01:46:09,040 --> 01:46:14,480
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With the indulgence of Honorable Tino, please proceed to your question and please wind up.

1173
01:46:14,480 --> 01:46:17,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I am, this is my last question.

1174
01:46:17,180 --> 01:46:24,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This is all related even to the appointment of Secretary Recto to be the Executive Secretary as he is now the acting.

1175
01:46:25,780 --> 01:46:28,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I guess acting kasi hindi naman pwede maibigay.

1176
01:46:28,560 --> 01:46:33,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang interim appointment because Congress is not in recess, diba?

1177
01:46:33,940 --> 01:46:37,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, okay. Anyway, ang sabi niya sa akin, hindi po totoo yan, Mr. Senator.

1178
01:46:37,940 --> 01:46:46,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kasi ang breakdown ng 100 billion, 81 billion yung na-assign sa DPWH, yung 29 billion other agencies.

1179
01:46:47,340 --> 01:46:55,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi niya alam, out of the 81 billion or out of the 100 billion, yung sa 81 billion, 52 billion siya ang personal na nag-handle.

1180
01:46:56,220 --> 01:46:57,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ako ang nag-handle noon.

1181
01:46:58,560 --> 01:47:01,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa notes niya, ito yung kanyang table.

1182
01:47:01,260 --> 01:47:06,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Binigyan niya na ako ng kopya, 51.01, I think, almost 52 billion.

1183
01:47:07,120 --> 01:47:10,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Anyway, sa 52 billion, yun yung personally hinandle niya.

1184
01:47:11,760 --> 01:47:19,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang talagang sabi niya, naghatid ako ng pera as kickback, but not to the President, but to Yusef Olaybar.

1185
01:47:20,080 --> 01:47:26,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang sabi niya, ang pagkakaalam niya, kasama si Adrian Bersamin, 8 billion pesos, Mr. President.

1186
01:47:26,980 --> 01:47:28,380
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With the indulgence of the Honorable Tino.

1187
01:47:28,560 --> 01:47:30,720
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Honorable Tino, please proceed to your question.

1188
01:47:31,200 --> 01:47:32,460
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Your time is up.

1189
01:47:32,460 --> 01:47:33,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito po yung question natin.

1190
01:47:33,520 --> 01:47:42,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The modus that day, yung arrangement nila is may tig-isa silang armored van, may armored van si Yusef Olaybar, may armored van siya.

1191
01:47:42,740 --> 01:47:45,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magpa-park sa basement ng Diamond Hotel.

1192
01:47:45,880 --> 01:47:52,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Darating yung van driven by Olaybar and possibly, sabi niya, hindi siya sigurado, and possibly along with Adrian Bersamin.

1193
01:47:53,260 --> 01:47:54,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakante yung armored van.

1194
01:47:54,520 --> 01:47:57,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ipa-park, idadrive yung isang van na puno ng pera.

1195
01:47:57,520 --> 01:47:58,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: With the indulgence

1196
01:47:58,560 --> 01:47:59,640
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: of the Honorable Tino.

1197
01:47:59,780 --> 01:48:02,460
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: What is your question so the sponsor can respond?

1198
01:48:04,160 --> 01:48:11,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Umabot sa 2 billion only because sometime in March, yung kanyang dati na sinabi from I think March hanggang April yung delivery.

1199
01:48:12,520 --> 01:48:21,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Anyway, ang sinabi ay, but personally he knows or he knew that kasi personally amounting to 8 billion.

1200
01:48:21,920 --> 01:48:24,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 1 billion he delivered to Secretary Punoan.

1201
01:48:24,840 --> 01:48:25,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So that's 9 billion.

1202
01:48:25,960 --> 01:48:28,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung 8 billion was representative of 16.

1203
01:48:28,560 --> 01:48:31,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung 8 billion was representative of 16 percent of the 81 billion.

1204
01:48:32,280 --> 01:48:34,160
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Thank you very much, Congressman Tino.

1205
01:48:34,360 --> 01:48:35,980
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Please go direct to the point.

1206
01:48:36,140 --> 01:48:38,460
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: What is your question so the sponsor can answer?

1207
01:48:38,660 --> 01:48:43,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang usapan daw nila initially was 15 percent for the President.

1208
01:48:44,160 --> 01:48:46,980
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Madam Speaker, the sponsor may respond please.

1209
01:48:46,980 --> 01:48:58,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Madam Speaker, ang tanong na po ay pagkatapos ng revelation nito on the records of the official records,

1210
01:48:58,400 --> 01:49:09,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the Senate in plenary delivered by Senator Lacson alleging na ganyan ang impormasyon na binigay ni Yusek Bernardo

1211
01:49:09,040 --> 01:49:15,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: na nag-deliver siya, may tinrabaho siyang 51 billion na insertions for the President

1212
01:49:15,240 --> 01:49:27,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: with a 16 percent kickback of 8 billion delivered through Yusek's Olaivar and Bersamin to the President.

1213
01:49:28,400 --> 01:49:34,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And after this, sinibak mo sa pwesto si Executive Secretary Bersamin,

1214
01:49:35,460 --> 01:49:38,520
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Pasensya na po, Congressman Tino, what is your question?

1215
01:49:38,680 --> 01:49:42,580
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Please go direct to the point because we have other interpellators online.

1216
01:49:42,580 --> 01:49:55,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit hanggang ngayon ay wala pa pong opisyal na paliwanag kung ba't sila sinibak at walang anumang investigasyon na pinapagawa ang Office of the President sa mga opisyal na ito?

1217
01:49:55,120 --> 01:49:55,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po ba pinagtatakpan?

1218
01:49:55,920 --> 01:49:57,860
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yes, Madam Speaker, if I may.

1219
01:49:58,400 --> 01:49:59,760
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Distinguished colleague.

1220
01:49:59,760 --> 01:50:02,200
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Congressman Tino, please let the sponsor respond.

1221
01:50:02,480 --> 01:50:03,660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The sponsor may proceed.

1222
01:50:04,160 --> 01:50:05,820
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Abet Garcia is recognized.

1223
01:50:06,500 --> 01:50:09,140
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The question is, are there investigations being conducted?

1224
01:50:10,720 --> 01:50:13,260
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yes, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleagues.

1225
01:50:13,420 --> 01:50:21,360
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: First of all, yung mga detalye po na nabanggit ng ating kasama, hindi po aware ang Office of the President with regards to those details.

1226
01:50:21,360 --> 01:50:27,660
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And with regards to investigation, yes, there are a lot of investigations being done.

1227
01:50:28,220 --> 01:50:28,360
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: By the way, I'm sorry.

1228
01:50:28,400 --> 01:50:36,580
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: By the Blue Ribbon Committee, by the Ombudsman, by the DOJ, at tuloy-tuloy po ang paggulong ng ating Pustisya.

1229
01:50:37,000 --> 01:50:57,400
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: In fact, ang dami na pong nakakulong ngayon, our former Speaker, Senator Jingoy, Senator Bong Revilla, Curly and Sara Diskaya, J.P. Mendoza, Roma Rimando, Henry Alcantara, Roberto Bernardo, Sally Santos,

1230
01:50:57,400 --> 01:51:00,500
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: at marami pa pong iba.

1231
01:51:01,080 --> 01:51:07,820
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, gumagulong po ang Pustisya sa ating bansa, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleagues.

1232
01:51:07,840 --> 01:51:08,400
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Maraming salamat.

1233
01:51:08,400 --> 01:51:14,340
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Maraming salamat, distinguished sponsor. Maraming salamat, Congressman Tino. Your time is up.

1234
01:51:14,500 --> 01:51:17,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker. Tapos na po ang aking interpellation.

1235
01:51:18,200 --> 01:51:25,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Let me just note that in the transcript as well, sabi dito, the President received the handwritten narration of Bernardo.

1236
01:51:25,660 --> 01:51:26,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, alam po niya ito.

1237
01:51:27,400 --> 01:51:30,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngunit hindi pa rin iniimbestigahan ng mga aligasyon dahil involved siya.

1238
01:51:31,240 --> 01:51:37,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, hindi pa po tapos ang paghahanap at pagpapanagot sa biggest fish ng flood control corruption scandal.

1239
01:51:37,400 --> 01:51:38,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker.

1240
01:51:38,200 --> 01:51:38,980
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

1241
01:51:39,920 --> 01:51:46,380
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Madam Speaker, I move to recognize the Honorable Egay Erice from the 2nd District of Caloocan to interpellate the sponsor.

1242
01:51:48,220 --> 01:51:55,380
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Egay Erice of the 2nd District of Caloocan City is hereby recognized for a very brief interpellation.

1243
01:51:57,400 --> 01:51:59,320
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

1244
01:52:02,100 --> 01:52:06,900
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Good morning to our Majority Leader and our sponsor.

1245
01:52:06,900 --> 01:52:19,400
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Madam Speaker, Mr. Chair, I recognize the proposed 10 billion budget of the Office of the President may be justified.

1246
01:52:20,540 --> 01:52:25,900
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And that it represents a substantial reduction from its 2026 allocation.

1247
01:52:27,400 --> 01:52:31,160
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: The reduction is as much as 64%.

1248
01:52:31,160 --> 01:52:36,500
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And I think with our problem in the West Philippine Sea,

1249
01:52:36,500 --> 01:52:44,960
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: a 4 billion intelligence fund, confidential fund is justified.

1250
01:52:46,120 --> 01:52:56,260
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: But my question concerns the policies that the President will pursue with approximately 21 months left before June 30.

1251
01:52:57,400 --> 01:53:02,780
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, may kasabihan tayong all's well that ends well.

1252
01:53:03,780 --> 01:53:12,040
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kaya ang pangunahing tanong ko po, paano balak ng administrasyon na matapos ng maayos

1253
01:53:12,040 --> 01:53:21,900
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: ang administrasyon at maiayos po ang gumabagal nating ekonomiya.

1254
01:53:23,560 --> 01:53:27,060
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Nais ko na rin pong samantalay ng pagkakataon.

1255
01:53:27,400 --> 01:53:40,080
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kung papaano po ang balak ng ating Pangulo upang iangat ang public spending, upang umangat ang ating ekonomiya.

1256
01:53:40,840 --> 01:53:51,800
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ganon din po kung ano ang mga hakbang na gagawin para bumaba po yung ating inflation, which is about 6%.

1257
01:53:51,800 --> 01:53:56,960
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ganon din po yung lumalaki nating pambansang utang.

1258
01:53:57,400 --> 01:54:06,220
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, kung paano po ang pagkakataon, siguro baka naman po may plano tayo kung paano natin medyo papagaanin ang pag-utang.

1259
01:54:06,380 --> 01:54:23,020
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: As I know that for the 2027 budget, we are about to borrow 1.69 trillion just to add another 1.6 trillion

1260
01:54:23,020 --> 01:54:34,510
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: para po sa ating mga maturing loans.

1261
01:54:36,480 --> 01:54:39,880
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Para po mapadali, sabihin ko na po lahat ng aking mga katanungan, then maybe you can answer.

1262
01:54:40,500 --> 01:54:45,220
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pagdating naman po sa reforms, sa reform agenda ng ating pamahalaan,

1263
01:54:46,180 --> 01:54:51,600
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: parang may nararamdaman po akong pushback doon sa pinangako ng ating Pangulo tungkol sa Kadena Act.

1264
01:54:52,780 --> 01:54:56,400
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ano po ba ang plano dito?

1265
01:54:57,400 --> 01:55:10,320
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ating administrasyon, ganoon din po sa alalabas lang na desisyon ng Korte Suprema

1266
01:55:10,320 --> 01:55:17,120
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: kung paano po irarali ng ating Pangulo ang anyang mga kaalyado sa Kongreso

1267
01:55:17,120 --> 01:55:23,300
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: para mapadali ang pagpapasa ng Anti-Political Dynasty Law.

1268
01:55:25,300 --> 01:55:26,560
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Iyon lamang po.

1269
01:55:27,400 --> 01:55:28,880
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Chair.

1270
01:55:41,180 --> 01:55:43,760
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

1271
01:55:44,340 --> 01:55:50,300
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: marami pong ginagawa ang ating Pangulo para umangat po yung ating ekonomiya.

1272
01:55:50,300 --> 01:55:57,300
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And of course, number one dito, yung pinaka-importanting legislation na ating ginagawa taon-taon,

1273
01:55:57,400 --> 01:56:03,720
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: which is the timely and quality passage of our budget.

1274
01:56:03,940 --> 01:56:11,320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Ang laki ng tulong po nito para sa government spending on time by the turn of the year,

1275
01:56:11,860 --> 01:56:16,040
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: nang sa ganoon ay lalo pang umangat ang ating GDP.

1276
01:56:16,660 --> 01:56:22,040
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: At the same time, nakita naman po natin na napaka-busy po ng ating Pangulo

1277
01:56:22,040 --> 01:56:26,520
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: in trying to attract foreign direct investment.

1278
01:56:26,520 --> 01:56:26,600
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay.

1279
01:56:27,400 --> 01:56:29,840
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Nung isang linggo, nasa India po siya.

1280
01:56:30,440 --> 01:56:37,580
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And there were commitments made by big businesses in India to invest in the Philippines.

1281
01:56:38,400 --> 01:56:46,880
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Kahapon, nakita po natin yung trade agreement signed by our Secretary of DTI with the EU,

1282
01:56:46,880 --> 01:56:52,680
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: which is, if I'm not mistaken, the third biggest economy in the world.

1283
01:56:53,340 --> 01:56:56,880
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: At mukhang susunod pa po ang isa pang trade agreement with Canada.

1284
01:56:57,400 --> 01:57:00,640
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, sa North America naman po, ito.

1285
01:57:01,080 --> 01:57:07,400
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, aside from government spending and attraction of foreign direct investment,

1286
01:57:08,060 --> 01:57:13,740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: hopefully, pag malampasan po natin itong energy crisis na ating pinagdadaanan

1287
01:57:13,740 --> 01:57:19,240
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: at ginagawan din po ng paraan ng ating Pangulo para maibsan itong crisis na ito

1288
01:57:19,240 --> 01:57:22,800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: sa pinagdadaanan ng ating mahamayan,

1289
01:57:23,500 --> 01:57:26,960
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: hopefully, tumaas na po at manumbalik yung sigla.

1290
01:57:27,400 --> 01:57:29,160
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Nang ating GDP.

1291
01:57:40,160 --> 01:57:45,540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And the Office of the President is confident with the timely passage of this budget,

1292
01:57:46,300 --> 01:57:52,260
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: babalik na tayo dun sa ating trajectory nung normal growth natin before the crisis began,

1293
01:57:52,260 --> 01:57:56,480
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: which is around 5, 5.5 to 6 percent.

1294
01:57:56,700 --> 01:57:57,260
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: ng ating GDP.

1295
01:57:59,040 --> 01:58:04,560
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And this will, of course, create a lot of jobs and opportunities for our country.

1296
01:58:23,440 --> 01:58:26,360
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: With regards to the management of our debt,

1297
01:58:26,360 --> 01:58:27,360
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker,

1298
01:58:27,960 --> 01:58:29,540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Honorable Colleague,

1299
01:58:30,220 --> 01:58:34,540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: pababa po ng pababa ang ating debt to GDP ratio.

1300
01:58:35,200 --> 01:58:38,520
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: A deficit to GDP ratio.

1301
01:58:39,440 --> 01:58:51,560
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, from 5.6 last year to 5.4 this year,

1302
01:58:52,260 --> 01:58:55,580
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and 4.8 by 2028.

1303
01:58:55,580 --> 01:58:56,580
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, pababa po yung...

1304
01:58:57,400 --> 01:59:00,880
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, pababa po yung deficit to GDP ratio.

1305
01:59:00,880 --> 01:59:07,380
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And we will maintain this trajectory para bumaba nang bumaba yung ratio.

1306
01:59:13,080 --> 01:59:17,240
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And because of that, Madam Speaker, Honorable Colleague,

1307
01:59:17,760 --> 01:59:22,520
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: by 2028, bababa na rin po yung debt to GDP ratio.

1308
01:59:23,560 --> 01:59:24,420
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Salamat po.

1309
01:59:24,560 --> 01:59:26,620
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yung pong reform agenda natin, yung kadena.

1310
01:59:26,740 --> 01:59:26,760
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yeah.

1311
01:59:26,760 --> 01:59:32,280
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: With regards to the Kadena Act, sinimula na po ng BBM.

1312
01:59:33,160 --> 01:59:39,800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Kung napapansin po ninyo yung kanyang programang entitled COMPASS,

1313
01:59:39,800 --> 01:59:47,560
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: or Centralized Open Monitoring Platform for Appropriation and Spending Statistics.

1314
01:59:47,960 --> 01:59:50,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Ito po yung nasa website ng BBM.

1315
01:59:51,400 --> 01:59:53,720
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: At nakita po po ito personally.

1316
01:59:54,360 --> 01:59:55,300
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Very informative.

1317
01:59:55,640 --> 01:59:56,620
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And this is open.

1318
01:59:56,760 --> 01:59:59,540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: To house members and everyone.

1319
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:03,980
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: para makita po natin yung spending ng ating gobyerno.

1320
02:00:04,380 --> 02:00:06,440
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And this is the first step to Kadena.

1321
02:00:06,960 --> 02:00:11,960
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Because once we digitalize, we now have the speed of light.

1322
02:00:12,280 --> 02:00:18,300
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Kumbaga, kahit sino pwede mag-download, pwede natin i-apply ang AI dito to analyze.

1323
02:00:18,920 --> 02:00:22,460
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: At kapag napasa na po ng both houses of Congress ang Kadena Act,

1324
02:00:22,980 --> 02:00:28,640
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: mas madali pong i-plug in dahil digitalize na po ang spending ng ating gobyerno.

1325
02:00:28,640 --> 02:00:39,400
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And this is my point, Mr. Speaker, that there's a pending bill in the House and the Senate regarding the Kadena Act.

1326
02:00:39,400 --> 02:00:46,620
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, ito po ba ay idideklara na urgent ng ating Pangulo?

1327
02:00:48,300 --> 02:00:55,460
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yes. The position of the President, he is supportive of this legislation.

1328
02:00:55,880 --> 02:00:58,540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: In fact, Madam Speaker, Honorable Colleague,

1329
02:00:58,640 --> 02:01:02,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: nasa ledak po itong legislation na ito.

1330
02:01:03,680 --> 02:01:10,100
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Kasama po siya sa isa, sa priority, legislative, executive priorities.

1331
02:01:11,220 --> 02:01:15,540
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Naipasa na rin po yung anti-political dynasty version ng House

1332
02:01:15,540 --> 02:01:20,720
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: at naipasa na rin po sa second reading, ang sa Senate.

1333
02:01:21,260 --> 02:01:28,620
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, may balak po ba ang Pangulo na maideclare na urgent ang anti-political dynasty?

1334
02:01:28,640 --> 02:01:38,460
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yes. Madam Speaker, Honorable Colleague,

1335
02:01:38,560 --> 02:01:44,680
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: I am quoting our Executive Secretary na he would like to take this opportunity

1336
02:01:44,680 --> 02:01:53,020
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: to address the House of Representatives and the Senate to pass this legislation.

1337
02:01:53,920 --> 02:01:57,000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: The President is very supportive of this bill.

1338
02:01:57,000 --> 02:01:58,000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker, Honorable Colleague.

1339
02:01:58,640 --> 02:02:01,040
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Thank you, Madam Chair.

1340
02:02:01,200 --> 02:02:02,340
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And for my last question,

1341
02:02:03,340 --> 02:02:09,200
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: basura, trapiko, pabahay at land use ang naguugnay na problema sa Metro Manila.

1342
02:02:09,780 --> 02:02:12,920
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 36% po ng GDP natin galing dito.

1343
02:02:13,660 --> 02:02:16,140
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: At kailangan-kailangan pong mabigyan ng solusyon.

1344
02:02:16,960 --> 02:02:22,660
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Bukas po ba ang Pangulo na supportahan ng isang elected Metropolitan Manila Government

1345
02:02:22,660 --> 02:02:26,260
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: sa ilalim ng Article 10, Section 11 ng ating Constitution

1346
02:02:26,260 --> 02:02:28,620
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: na nagpapahintulot sa Congress?

1347
02:02:28,640 --> 02:02:33,160
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, na lumika ng Special Metropolitan Political Subdivision

1348
02:02:33,160 --> 02:02:36,080
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: nasa sa ilalim sa isang plebisito?

1349
02:02:37,880 --> 02:02:40,480
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Madam Speaker, Honorable Colleague,

1350
02:02:40,980 --> 02:02:47,940
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: ang ating Executive Secretary have not discussed this particular issue with the President,

1351
02:02:48,420 --> 02:02:53,500
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: pero according to our ES, he thinks this is a good idea.

1352
02:02:54,380 --> 02:02:54,880
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Salamat po.

1353
02:02:54,880 --> 02:02:56,900
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: In this case, in behalf of the minority,

1354
02:02:57,760 --> 02:02:58,380
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: I move.

1355
02:02:58,380 --> 02:03:03,760
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, to terminate the discussion on the budget of the Office of the President.

1356
02:03:04,240 --> 02:03:04,720
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, move.

1357
