Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Mr. Speaker, I move that we consider the proposed budget of the Presidential Communications Office, PCO.

1416
02:09:35,920 --> 02:09:36,460
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: Please proceed.

1417
02:09:37,500 --> 02:09:45,440
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Mr. Speaker, may we acknowledge the heads of the officials of the Presidential Communications Office.

1418
02:09:45,440 --> 02:09:55,560
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Secretary M. Gomez, Undersecretary of Ruth Abigail Testoso, Undersecretary Ramon Ilagan,

1419
02:09:56,540 --> 02:09:57,440
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Office of In Charge Alan...

1420
02:09:58,380 --> 02:09:59,380
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Alinig...

1421
02:09:59,380 --> 02:10:00,380
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Alinig...

1422
02:10:00,380 --> 02:10:23,640
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Alianigue, Office of In Charge Arlene Barrientos, Director Nicole Bacolod, Office of In Charge Jericho Paloma, Assistant Director General Christine Bennett Andal,

1423
02:10:23,640 --> 02:10:27,640
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: President CEO Jose Policarpo.

1424
02:10:28,380 --> 02:10:39,320
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Junior, Network General Management Manager, Dino C. Cayetano, President Gil Carlo Puyat.

1425
02:10:41,520 --> 02:10:45,020
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: To our guests from the Presidential Communications Office,

1426
02:10:45,680 --> 02:10:48,640
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: led by Ad interim Secretary Dave M. Gomez,

1427
02:10:49,340 --> 02:10:50,900
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: welcome to the House of Representatives.

1428
02:10:52,900 --> 02:10:54,020
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: Majority Leader?

1429
02:10:55,760 --> 02:10:57,080
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Mr. Speaker?

1430
02:10:58,380 --> 02:11:17,280
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: I move that we recognize Vice Chairperson Queenie Gonzales of the Lone District of Mandaluyong to sponsor the proposed budget of the Presidential Communications Office.

1431
02:11:18,420 --> 02:11:21,780
Deputy Speaker Francisco Paolo P. Ortega V: The Honorable Gonzales is now recognized. You may proceed.

1432
02:11:23,500 --> 02:11:26,920
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues, good morning.

1433
02:11:28,380 --> 02:11:35,720
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: It is an honor and privilege to sponsor the proposed 2.62 billion budget of the Presidential Communications Office

1434
02:11:35,720 --> 02:11:41,700
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: and its attached agencies and corporations for fiscal year 2027.

1435
02:11:42,320 --> 02:11:45,580
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: As the lead communications arm of the government,

1436
02:11:46,160 --> 02:11:53,300
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: the PCO plays a vital role in ensuring that the Filipino people receive timely, accurate, accessible,

1437
02:11:53,300 --> 02:11:57,940
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: and responsible information on government policies, programs,

1438
02:11:57,940 --> 02:11:58,940
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: and services.

1439
02:11:58,940 --> 02:12:08,180
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: We have the lowest budget and the last department-level agency of the Executive Department in terms of budgetary allocation.

1440
02:12:08,180 --> 02:12:27,540
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: PCO may have the least budget priority, but they assure your honors that they are up to the Herculean task of engaging and involving the citizenry and the mass media in enriching the quality of public discourse on all matters of governance.

1441
02:12:27,540 --> 02:12:30,440
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: This function is essential to good governance.

1442
02:12:30,920 --> 02:12:45,240
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Government programs can serve the public only when citizens understand what assistance is available, how to access it, why policies are being adopted, and how public institutions may be held accountable.

1443
02:12:46,060 --> 02:12:54,780
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Clear communication, therefore, connects policy with public service, supports participation, and helps sustain trust between the government and the people.

1444
02:12:54,780 --> 02:12:57,520
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: This responsibility has become

1445
02:12:57,520 --> 02:13:03,340
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: even more significant at a time when social media is woven into everyday life.

