Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: at misalignment ng pricing timelines sa academic calendar.

3501
04:02:08,280 --> 04:02:09,860
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Pero sa mga delays po na ito,

3502
04:02:10,160 --> 04:02:13,280
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: alin po dito ang pangunahing ina-address ng CHED reforms?

3503
04:02:17,880 --> 04:02:21,720
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Ang priority of course is direct distribution.

3504
04:02:22,360 --> 04:02:24,860
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Actually, we have here with us in real time

3505
04:02:24,860 --> 04:02:25,620
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: kung ilan na yung

3506
04:02:25,640 --> 04:02:26,960
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: nabigyan,

3507
04:02:26,960 --> 04:02:29,340
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: ilan yung mino-monitor.

3508
04:02:29,480 --> 04:02:33,480
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: So complete naman po actually with all the digital information ng CHED.

3509
04:02:34,580 --> 04:02:36,260
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Maraming salamat, Madam Sponsor.

3510
04:02:36,380 --> 04:02:42,160
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Umaasa po tayo sa CHED na mapabilis at mapapaiting po nila ang scholarship processing

3511
04:02:42,160 --> 04:02:45,520
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: upang ang financial assistance ay matatanggap ng mga estudyante

3512
04:02:45,520 --> 04:02:47,400
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: sa panahon tunay na ito po ay kailangan.

3513
04:02:48,220 --> 04:02:51,940
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Ang pang-apat na katanungan ko po, Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor,

3514
04:02:51,940 --> 04:02:55,200
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: ay may kinalangan man po sa actual cost of tertiary education access.

3515
04:02:55,640 --> 04:03:13,800
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor, para sa mga estudyanteng galing sa geographically isolated or low-income communities, tuition may already be covered pero ang transportation, boarding, pagkain, books, and connectivity remain major expenses.

3516
04:03:14,200 --> 04:03:21,040
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Paano po kinukonsider ng CHED ang mga non-tuition barriers sa pag-access at pagkatapos ng college?

3517
04:03:27,440 --> 04:03:44,640
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Yes. Ang isa pang programa na bago sa ating CHED, they signed a MOA with Pag-ibig for the Balay which should help with accommodations with the construction of dormitories.

3518
04:03:49,400 --> 04:03:54,820
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Madam Sponsor, may geographic or regional data po ba ang CHED kung saan pinakamataas ang dropout?

3519
04:03:54,820 --> 04:03:59,020
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Or non-completion dahil sa living education related costs?

3520
04:04:20,740 --> 04:04:24,160
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Yes. If you need the data, may we submit this to you na lang po.

3521
04:04:24,160 --> 04:04:24,460
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Thank you.

3522
04:04:24,820 --> 04:04:26,440
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Thank you, Madam Sponsor.

3523
04:04:27,520 --> 04:04:34,300
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: So, mahalaga po ito, Madam Sponsor, kahit libre ang tuition, hindi libre ang buong cost of going to college.

3524
04:04:34,300 --> 04:04:47,680
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Para sa mga estudyanteng malayo sa kanilang paralan, umula sa low-income families, maaaring ang gasto sa pamasahe, tirahan, pagkain, books, at internet ang maging dahilan kung bakit nahirapan silang mag-enroll at magpatuloy hanggang makagraduate.

3525
04:04:47,940 --> 04:04:54,800
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor, para sa maraming pamilyang Pilipino, malaking investment ang pag-aaral ng anak.

3526
04:04:54,820 --> 04:05:06,860
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Kaya, mahalaga po na ang tulong ng gobyerno mula sa scholarship hanggang sa pag-atid ng quality education ay talagang nakakatulong sa estudyanteng hanggang siya ay makapagtapos at magkaroon ng trabaho.

3527
04:05:07,360 --> 04:05:18,800
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Hangad po natin na mas mapalakas pa ng CHED ang mga programa, reforma, at serbisyo na tutugon sa tunay na pangailangan ng mga estudyante at maganda sa kanila para sa maraming oportunidad at magandang kinabukasan.

3528
04:05:18,900 --> 04:05:21,320
Rep. Jernie Jett V. Nisay: Maraming salamat po, Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor.

3529
04:05:21,840 --> 04:05:23,740
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Thank you, Honorable Nisoy, Majority Leader.

3530
04:05:24,820 --> 04:05:36,300
Rep. Ma. Alana Samantha Taliño Santos: Mr. Speaker, I move that we recognize Honorable Dada Kiram Ismula of Akbayan Partylist to interpret the budget of the Commission of Higher Education.

3531
04:05:36,800 --> 04:05:42,360
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The Honorable Dada Kiram Ismula of Partylist Akbayan is recognized. Please proceed.

3532
04:05:44,020 --> 04:05:46,360
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Assalamualaikum, Murahmatullahi Wabarakatuhu.

3533
04:05:47,280 --> 04:05:53,680
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor, noong nakaraang taon sa budget deliberations para sa CHED,

3534
04:05:53,680 --> 04:05:59,580
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: na itanong natin kung merong datos ang CHED sa dropout rate ng mga IPs.

3535
04:06:00,220 --> 04:06:06,860
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Natanggap po natin ang liham ng CHED last year na nagsasabing walang available na datos dito.

3536
04:06:07,660 --> 04:06:19,400
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maliban dito sa IP dropout rates, can I confirm kung may datos na ba ang CHED para sa indigenous people, student, enrollment, retention, and graduation?

3537
04:06:23,680 --> 04:06:30,340
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Sige po.

3538
04:06:31,360 --> 04:06:38,040
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Taking off from your question last year, kung kaya't inumpisahan po ng CHED,

3539
04:06:38,600 --> 04:06:43,300
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: i-gather your information at the moment, ongoing pa rin po.

3540
04:06:44,100 --> 04:06:51,420
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Pero ang meron po tayo that we can inform our good colleague, yung pong number of scholars.

3541
04:06:51,420 --> 04:06:51,700
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Yes.

3542
04:06:53,680 --> 04:07:02,700
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: For 2025, may 226.

3543
04:07:06,080 --> 04:07:08,720
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: And for 2026, we have 205.

3544
04:07:11,500 --> 04:07:17,320
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor, naitanong ko po ito dahil gusto ko lang maging consistent, no?

3545
04:07:17,320 --> 04:07:23,320
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At gusto ko lang din makita na talagang tinatrabaho na ito ng CHED na i-integrate.

3546
04:07:23,680 --> 04:07:29,640
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Or isama na rin talaga sa datos ng CHED yung patungkol sa mga IP datas.

3547
04:07:30,580 --> 04:07:38,240
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At dahil wala pa sa ngayon, kaugnay ng aking naunang katanungan sa liham din ng CHED,

3548
04:07:38,240 --> 04:07:45,540
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: they committed to issue a memorandum that will require HEIs to submit IP student profile.

3549
04:07:46,460 --> 04:07:53,520
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor, maari ko po bang i-confirm ma ang commitment na ito if this has been complied with?

3550
04:07:53,680 --> 04:08:00,020
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Dahil ang opisina ko po ay hindi pa rin naka-receive, kaugnay dito sa memorandum na ito.

3551
04:08:00,300 --> 04:08:00,580
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Yes.

3552
04:08:00,580 --> 04:08:11,480
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At kung ating pong babalikan yung last year, mismo dito rin po sa plenary, kinomit ng Secretary of CHED yung memorandum na iyon.

3553
04:08:11,640 --> 04:08:11,880
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Yes.

3554
04:08:13,460 --> 04:08:22,240
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: As an answer to that, taking off from last year's inquiry, we have, the CHED has a summary total enrollment and graduates per region.

3555
04:08:22,400 --> 04:08:23,660
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: So meron po tayong dato.

3556
04:08:23,680 --> 04:08:28,860
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: At willing po ang CHED na i-furnish po ang opisina nyo ng kopya na ito.

3557
04:08:29,100 --> 04:08:30,120
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat po.

3558
04:08:30,200 --> 04:08:34,240
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At kung maaari, i-follow up ko na rin po yung memorandum na iyon.

3559
04:08:34,800 --> 04:08:44,800
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Dahil ito'y binanggit po mismo ng Secretary during the budget briefing nung nakaraang taon na pagkatapos na pagkatapos ng budget briefing,

3560
04:08:45,280 --> 04:08:47,800
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ay i-release niya ang memorandum na iyon.

3561
04:08:53,680 --> 04:09:00,600
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At kung sakaling hindi pa po nakapag-release ng memorandum, itatanong ko na lang po,

3562
04:09:00,940 --> 04:09:04,540
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: kailan po kaya mag-i-issue ang CHED ng memorandum na ito?

3563
04:09:05,160 --> 04:09:10,860
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At paano nila masisiguro na ito ay susundin ng ating mga HEIs?

3564
04:09:12,440 --> 04:09:13,040
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Yes.

3565
04:09:13,360 --> 04:09:16,440
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Kaya po nakuha yung datos ay dahil naglabas ng memo.

3566
04:09:16,440 --> 04:09:22,440
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: But at any rate, ang karagdaga na ginawa po dyan is under the student records managerial,

3567
04:09:23,680 --> 04:09:28,360
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: management system, may IP profiling. Kasama na po siya.

3568
04:09:28,640 --> 04:09:31,220
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, Madam Sponsor.

3569
04:09:32,020 --> 04:09:39,960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Kaya ko po naitanong ang tungkol sa datos na ito para masiguro na natutugunan ang mga concerns ng ating mga HEIs.

3570
04:09:39,960 --> 04:09:46,960
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ngayong hindi pa kompleto ang mga datos o kakasimula pa lang at continuous pa ito,

3571
04:09:47,880 --> 04:09:52,360
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: paano po kaya nasisiguro ng CHED na ang budget at mga programa

3572
04:09:52,360 --> 04:09:58,460
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ay talagang nakakarating at nakakatulong sa mga IP students na nangangailangan?

3573
04:10:04,280 --> 04:10:05,160
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Sige po.

3574
04:10:06,600 --> 04:10:14,820
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: The CHED will enter into a MOA with the LGUs to be able to help them monitor.

3575
04:10:15,560 --> 04:10:19,680
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: But because they are now part of the profiling system of the school,

3576
04:10:19,680 --> 04:10:21,680
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: they are sure to receive all the...

3577
04:10:22,360 --> 04:10:24,460
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: All the benefits that they should from the CHED.

3578
04:10:24,800 --> 04:10:26,820
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, Madam Sponsor.

3579
04:10:27,240 --> 04:10:30,720
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Humihingi na lamang po ako ng kopya ng memorandum na ito.

3580
04:10:31,100 --> 04:10:39,820
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At kung maaari po, hingi na rin po ako ng datos na available mula sa CHED sa datos ng patungkol sa IP.

3581
04:10:40,260 --> 04:10:40,700
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Sige po.

3582
04:10:41,920 --> 04:10:48,360
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Across all regions, merong 21,953 IPs na nakikinabang.

3583
04:10:49,300 --> 04:10:49,980
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat.

3584
04:10:49,980 --> 04:10:52,120
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: We will share the same data with you.

3585
04:10:52,360 --> 04:10:53,380
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Yes. Maraming salamat po.

3586
04:10:53,480 --> 04:10:55,760
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: On the matter of indigenous people's studies,

3587
04:10:55,760 --> 04:11:01,820
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: we note CHED Memorandum Order No. 2, Series of 2019,

3588
04:11:02,500 --> 04:11:07,000
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: which mandates the integration of IP studies.

3589
04:11:08,140 --> 04:11:17,160
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ano ang budget allocated for 2027 para i-ensure ang full implementation and monitoring of IP studies integration?

3590
04:11:18,440 --> 04:11:22,340
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Ang ongoing po for IP studies integration sa curriculum,

3591
04:11:22,360 --> 04:11:29,320
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: is 5.578,250 million, which is part of the request of the CHED.

3592
04:11:29,840 --> 04:11:30,600
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat.

3593
04:11:30,700 --> 04:11:36,480
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sa latest data available, ilang HEIs na ang nakipag-integrate ng IP studies?

3594
04:11:37,240 --> 04:11:43,820
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ano ang mga balakid para sa ibang HEIs na i-implement ng IP studies integration?

3595
04:11:46,380 --> 04:11:49,580
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Yes. Status of this is ongoing.

3596
04:11:49,580 --> 04:11:52,340
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Kailangan lang po talaga with the limited manpower.

3597
04:11:52,360 --> 04:11:59,480
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Nag-dedistribute lang po minimally ng mga tao in all the needs na kailangan ni-monitor.

3598
04:11:59,600 --> 04:12:02,600
Rep. Monique Yazmin Maria Q. Lagdameo: Pero definitely ongoing po ang monitoring ng CHED.

3599
04:12:03,300 --> 04:12:05,400
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat, Madam Sponsor.

3600
04:12:05,800 --> 04:12:09,240
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At itong representasyong ito magiging consistent next year.

3601
04:12:09,620 --> 04:12:10,080
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: See you.

3602
04:12:10,580 --> 04:12:14,680
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At the same pa rin po ang aking magiging katanungan sa CHED.

3603
04:12:15,440 --> 04:12:19,540
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: And anyways, I think wala na po mula sa minority.

3604
04:12:20,340 --> 04:12:22,340
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Mr. Speaker, Madam.

3605
04:12:22,360 --> 04:12:33,120
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Madam Sponsor, since there is no remaining member of the minority who wishes to interpolate on the proposed 2027 budget of the Commission on Higher Education,

3606
04:12:33,880 --> 04:12:44,360
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I move that we terminate the period of sponsorship debates and interpolations for the 2027 proposed budget of the Commission on Higher Education.

3607
04:12:44,660 --> 04:12:45,200
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: So move.

3608
04:12:45,760 --> 04:12:47,400
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: What does the House say, Majority Leader?

3609
04:12:48,400 --> 04:12:57,200
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Mr. Speaker, on part of the majority, we join the minority in the motion to terminate the period of sponsorship debates and interpolations for the 2027 proposed budget of the Commission on Higher Education.

3610
04:12:57,360 --> 04:13:06,880
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: There is a joint motion to terminate the interpolations on the proposed budget of the Commission on Higher Education.

3611
04:13:08,160 --> 04:13:11,560
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Is there any objection? The chair here is none.

3612
04:13:12,120 --> 04:13:17,720
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The interpolations on the proposed budget of the Commission on Higher Education is terminated.

3613
04:13:18,800 --> 04:13:19,640
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Congratulations.

3614
04:13:19,640 --> 04:13:20,120
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Congratulations.

3615
04:13:20,120 --> 04:13:25,860
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Majority Leader.

3616
04:13:26,320 --> 04:13:28,860
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, I move to suspend session for a few minutes.

3617
04:13:29,020 --> 04:13:29,900
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Session is suspended.

3618
04:19:44,550 --> 04:19:46,400
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Session is resumed. Majority Leader.

3619
04:19:46,400 --> 04:19:49,600
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, I move to consider the proposed budget of the state universities and colleges.

3620
04:19:49,600 --> 04:19:54,100
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Is there any objection? The Chair hears none. Motion is approved. Majority Leader.

3621
04:19:54,100 --> 04:19:59,980
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, may we acknowledge the heads and officials of the state universities and colleges?

3622
04:20:00,000 --> 04:20:36,470
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: PASUC President Dr. Tirso [unclear], Vice President for NCR Dr. Bert Tuga, Vice President for Luzon Dr. Silverio Ramon [unclear], Vice President for Visayas Dr. Norberto Mangulabnan, Vice President for Mindanao Dr. Joy Capistrano, UP President Attorney Angelo Jimenez, Philippine General Hospital Dr. Gerardo Legaspi, UP Resilience Institute Dr. Alo Mahar Lagay, and all presidents of the state universities and colleges.

3623
04:20:37,250 --> 04:21:02,880
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: To the family of the state universities and colleges in the Philippines, led by Dr. [unclear], PASUC President; Dr. Robert J. [unclear], Vice President for NCR; Dr. Silverio Ramon [unclear], Vice President for Luzon; Dr. Norberto Mangulabnan, Vice President for Visayas.

3624
04:21:02,920 --> 04:21:29,980
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Dr. Joy Capistrano, Vice President for Mindanao; Attorney Angelo Jimenez, UP President; Dr. Gerardo Legaspi, Director of Philippine General Hospital; Dr. Alfredo Maharlagmay, Director of UP Resilience Institute; and all the presidents of the state universities and colleges. We gladly welcome you to the House of Representatives.

3625
04:21:30,000 --> 04:21:31,570
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Majority Leader.

3626
04:21:31,570 --> 04:21:45,480
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Karl Fernandez Legazpi, Vice Chairperson of the Committee on Appropriations, to sponsor the proposed budget of the state universities and colleges.

3627
04:21:45,480 --> 04:21:53,240
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The Honorable Vice Chair Karl Fernandez Legazpi of Partylist Pinoy Workers is recognized. Please proceed.

3628
04:21:53,240 --> 04:21:59,980
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues, I rise today to sponsor the proposed fiscal year 2027 budgets of our state universities and colleges.

3629
04:22:00,000 --> 04:22:29,980
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Across the country, including the University of the Philippines system. At the outset, Mr. Speaker, I acknowledge my fellow sponsors who will help defend SUC budgets in their respective areas: Representative Arthur Celeste for Luzon, Representative Emer Lollipop [unclear] and Representative Karl Nicolas [unclear] for the Visayas.

3630
04:22:30,000 --> 04:22:59,980
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: And Representative Bernadette Barbers and Representative [unclear] for SUCs in Mindanao. I thank our co-sponsors for taking on this responsibility and helping ensure the concerns and requirements of our state universities and colleges across the country are represented before this House. It is a particular honor for me to stand here on behalf of my own alma mater, the University of the Philippines.

3631
04:23:00,000 --> 04:23:29,980
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: But today we speak not only for one university or one region. Together we speak for the students of our state universities and colleges from Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao, young Filipinos who look to public higher education as their pathway to a better life. Para sa maraming pamilyang Pilipino, ang makapasok sa isang pampublikong unibersidad ay higit pa sa pagtanggap ng diploma. Ito ay pagkakataon na makapagtapos para sa kanilang kinabukasan at sa kinabukasan ng kanilang mga pamilya.

3632
04:23:30,000 --> 04:23:59,980
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Sa bawat pintuang binubuksan ng ating mga SUCs, may pamilyang nabibigyan ng pagkakataong mangarap nang mas malaki. Iyan ang pangakong dala ng ating mga SUCs. Under the proposed fiscal year 2027 national budget, our state universities and colleges are allocated 141.09 billion, an increase of 6.1 billion or 4.5% compared with the fiscal year 2026 National Expenditure Program.

3633
04:24:00,000 --> 04:24:29,980
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Funding for the Universal Access to Quality Tertiary Education program is likewise being increased as more Filipino students enter our public universities. But our responsibility does not end with opening the doors of our universities. Access must come with quality. As enrollment grows, our SUCs must have enough teachers, classrooms, laboratories, equipment, and learning resources.

3634
04:24:30,000 --> 04:24:31,000
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Our campuses

3635
04:24:31,000 --> 04:24:32,000
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: must be safe

3636
04:24:32,000 --> 04:24:33,000
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: and capable

3637
04:24:33,000 --> 04:24:34,000
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: of supporting

3638
04:24:34,000 --> 04:24:35,000
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: the students

3639
04:24:35,000 --> 04:24:36,000
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: who depend on them.

3640
04:24:36,000 --> 04:24:37,000
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Our faculty

3641
04:24:37,000 --> 04:24:38,000
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: must be given

