4389
05:06:04,380 --> 05:06:07,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Rizal Technological University, 39 million.

4390
05:06:08,320 --> 05:06:10,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bicol University, 32 million.

4391
05:06:10,360 --> 05:06:11,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung po yung top 5.

4392
05:06:11,260 --> 05:06:13,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: E ba, magiging ko na rin PUP.

4393
05:06:13,140 --> 05:06:16,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: MOUE, 26.3 million cut.

4394
05:06:17,260 --> 05:06:22,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Also, I can mention, Don Mariano Marcos Memorial State University,

4395
05:06:22,300 --> 05:06:25,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yan ang pinanggalingan, former president, yung chair-chair mismo,

4396
05:06:26,180 --> 05:06:29,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: may cut din po na 20 million sa kanilang MOUE.

4397
05:06:29,680 --> 05:06:33,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, magkano po ang kailangan na dagdag para sa MOUE, if ever?

4398
05:07:10,240 --> 05:07:13,040
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Madam Speaker and distinguished colleague,

4399
05:07:13,140 --> 05:07:17,120
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ang nilalais po yung balik ng ating pasok, ating mga university and colleges,

4400
05:07:17,640 --> 05:07:26,400
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: ay yung 20% lang po na natanggal sa kanilang MOUE budget na nirequest po nila for the 2027 NEP po.

4401
05:07:26,960 --> 05:07:35,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, in other words, masaya na ang SUC sa kung ano yung level noong 2026

4402
05:07:35,020 --> 05:07:40,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at huwag ibawas yung 20% na cut.

4403
05:07:41,820 --> 05:07:42,620
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Yes po.

4404
05:07:43,140 --> 05:07:45,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ito po ang kahilingan nila, Madam Speaker.

4405
05:07:45,620 --> 05:07:50,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Let me just note na because of the energy emergency,

4406
05:07:51,580 --> 05:08:00,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay nag-utos ang DepEd na isoli daw ng mga SUC yung 20% ng kanilang MOUE.

4407
05:08:01,480 --> 05:08:06,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, parang naging forced savings ito at mukhang ito yung ginamit para ma-augment yung pang-ayuda, diba pa?

4408
05:08:07,780 --> 05:08:10,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Actually, nakarating po yan sa atin.

4409
05:08:10,920 --> 05:08:13,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi ng mga faculty and staff,

4410
05:08:13,140 --> 05:08:19,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: na kinaltasan ng malaki yung MOUE, kaya wala na raw pang kahit nagtitipid sila.

4411
05:08:20,220 --> 05:08:25,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alinsunod sa CNA agreement, Collective Negotiation Agreements,

4412
05:08:25,820 --> 05:08:31,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sinasabi po sa kanila ngayon mukhang walang mapagkukunan ng savings

4413
05:08:31,160 --> 05:08:37,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: that are supposed to be the source of funding for the CNA incentive.

4414
05:08:38,220 --> 05:08:41,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, we're bringing that concern here.

4415
05:08:42,020 --> 05:08:42,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4416
05:08:42,660 --> 05:08:44,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And also, yun na nga.

4417
05:08:45,020 --> 05:08:49,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi na, sinusuportahan natin ng panawagan na sa minimum, ibalik yung mga cut.

4418
05:08:50,900 --> 05:08:54,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi bumaba dun sa 2027 level, dapat madagdagan pa.

4419
05:08:55,080 --> 05:09:00,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How about capital outlay, Mr. Speaker, Madam Speaker, Mr. Sponsor?

4420
05:09:01,020 --> 05:09:07,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Balita ko, may mga state universities na zero pa nga ang capital outlay.

4421
05:09:07,880 --> 05:09:11,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Naintindihan natin, sabihin nila, hindi naman pwedeng pareho lang nung

4422
05:09:11,540 --> 05:09:16,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2026 ang capital outlay. One time yan eh.

4423
05:09:17,040 --> 05:09:23,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pero meron pong narinig tayo na a number of SUCs, zero pa nga ang capital outlay.

4424
05:09:23,980 --> 05:09:24,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba yun?

4425
05:09:25,460 --> 05:09:27,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po yun, Madam Speaker.

4426
05:09:27,720 --> 05:09:30,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilang state universities ang walang capital outlay?

4427
05:09:30,220 --> 05:09:34,380
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Based on the data submitted sa data sa binigay ng PASOK,

4428
05:09:34,460 --> 05:09:40,220
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: nasa 12 po, 12 ang SUCs na wala pong capital outlay sa kanilang...

4429
05:09:40,220 --> 05:09:44,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 12 SUCs. Pwede po ba natin marinig for the record?

4430
05:09:45,880 --> 05:09:49,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sino yung 12 SUCs na walang capital outlay?

4431
05:09:56,740 --> 05:10:00,600
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: At pinapadagdag din po ng ating PASOK na...

4432
05:10:00,600 --> 05:10:00,760
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Sige po.

4433
05:10:02,260 --> 05:10:09,360
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ano po, tumaas pa ang numero, nasa 25 po na SUCs ang walang infrastructure projects.

4434
05:10:10,220 --> 05:10:15,620
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: So, yung kanina pong 12, ayun po ay ano lang yun, no capital outlay allocation.

4435
05:10:16,020 --> 05:10:18,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, yung absolutely zero?

4436
05:10:18,740 --> 05:10:20,080
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Opo, tama po yun, Madam Speaker.

4437
05:10:20,080 --> 05:10:24,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon, 25 kung walang infrastructure projects.

4438
05:10:24,900 --> 05:10:27,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, maaring may capital outlay pero hindi infrastructure.

4439
05:10:27,860 --> 05:10:28,200
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Tama po.

4440
05:10:28,220 --> 05:10:32,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun ang ibig sabihin nun. Okay. Para marinig lang natin, sino yung 12 na yan?

4441
05:10:33,320 --> 05:10:37,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Para nasa record at para mabantayan natin kung magkakaroon pa rin ba.

4442
05:10:38,340 --> 05:10:40,080
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Maari po namin i-furnish po.

4443
05:10:40,220 --> 05:10:44,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O, sige. Gusto sana natin ilagay sa record. Pero, sige na po. Okay.

4444
05:10:46,560 --> 05:10:50,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pahingi na lang, nung listahan ng 12 and the 25 na binabanggit ninyo,

4445
05:10:51,260 --> 05:10:53,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: para ma-follow up din natin, mabantayan.

4446
05:10:54,040 --> 05:10:55,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No? Okay.

4447
05:10:56,100 --> 05:11:00,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Next, plantilla items. Plantilla positions.

4448
05:11:00,960 --> 05:11:02,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Particularly for faculty.

4449
05:11:02,400 --> 05:11:09,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam natin may ongoing na programa para makapag-hire ng...

4450
05:11:10,220 --> 05:11:13,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: administrative or non-teaching positions.

4451
05:11:14,160 --> 05:11:17,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, let us take a look at faculty items.

4452
05:11:18,120 --> 05:11:19,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilan po ngayon?

4453
05:11:19,460 --> 05:11:23,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil po sa free higher education, naturally, lumalaki ang enrollment.

4454
05:11:24,560 --> 05:11:28,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At naturally, kailangan mo ng mas maraming teachers, faculty.

4455
05:11:29,600 --> 05:11:33,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero, hindi naman po nagdadagdag ng new items.

4456
05:11:33,580 --> 05:11:37,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Therefore, job order and contract of service faculty.

4457
05:11:37,560 --> 05:11:38,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilan na po ngayon?

4458
05:11:40,220 --> 05:11:43,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang mga faculty na job order and contract of service.

4459
05:11:49,460 --> 05:11:51,540
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

4460
05:11:51,920 --> 05:11:57,600
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: nasa 55,000 po ang ating mga job order and contract of service workers

4461
05:11:57,600 --> 05:12:03,280
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: na kabilang po sa part-time faculty ng ating mga SUCs sa buong Pilipinas.

4462
05:12:03,300 --> 05:12:09,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, 55,000 job order. Lahat yan, faculty. Tama po. Is that correct?

4463
05:12:10,220 --> 05:12:13,200
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Sama na po yung teaching and non-teaching items po dito.

4464
05:12:13,240 --> 05:12:16,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Teaching and non-teaching. Well, pwede po bang mabigyan tayo?

4465
05:12:16,700 --> 05:12:20,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mukhang wala kayong datos. Ilan dito yung teaching, ilan yung non-teaching?

4466
05:12:26,420 --> 05:12:29,080
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Sa lukuyin po, wala pong current breakdown.

4467
05:12:29,080 --> 05:12:31,080
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Pero, ano po, they will...

4468
05:12:33,440 --> 05:12:40,080
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ang informasyon po na binigyan ng PASOK, 26,000 po ang teaching positions.

4469
05:12:40,220 --> 05:12:42,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Out of the 55?

4470
05:12:42,640 --> 05:12:44,480
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Na ano po, na job order.

4471
05:12:45,020 --> 05:12:49,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, 26,000. Ayan po, malinaw na malinaw ah.

4472
05:12:49,540 --> 05:12:57,060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 26,000 faculty or teaching positions na job order or contract of service.

4473
05:12:59,140 --> 05:13:02,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Obviously, malaking injustice ito.

4474
05:13:02,800 --> 05:13:09,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, tutulak din po natin na mabigyan ng bagong items,

4475
05:13:09,280 --> 05:13:11,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang mga state universities and colleges,

4476
05:13:12,500 --> 05:13:14,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: katulad nung naipanalo natin noong 2016,

4477
05:13:15,680 --> 05:13:22,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: where 9,000 items were created and distributed to the state universities and colleges.

4478
05:13:22,500 --> 05:13:27,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kahit pa pano, at the time, that was one-third of the requirement.

4479
05:13:28,400 --> 05:13:33,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kahit pa pano, nakatulong. Hopefully, magawa uli natin ngayong taon.

4480
05:13:35,300 --> 05:13:37,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Practically a decade after that.

4481
05:13:37,380 --> 05:13:37,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

4482
05:13:38,740 --> 05:13:39,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

4483
05:13:39,280 --> 05:13:40,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, malinaw po ito.

4484
05:13:41,060 --> 05:13:41,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Last point.

4485
05:13:43,120 --> 05:13:43,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Last point.

4486
05:13:44,200 --> 05:13:49,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I actually already made this point during the interpolation of CHED, the CHED budget.

4487
05:13:50,320 --> 05:13:54,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, gusto po natin marinig ito ng ating mga state universities and colleges,

4488
05:13:54,560 --> 05:13:56,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and for the record, in plenary as well,

4489
05:13:57,640 --> 05:14:01,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yung babalikan ko yung advokasya natin ngayon, no?

4490
05:14:02,020 --> 05:14:07,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ng injustice to instructor one position.

4491
05:14:07,580 --> 05:14:09,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung mga instructor one.

4492
05:14:09,280 --> 05:14:12,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung mga instructor one position natin sa state universities and colleges.

4493
05:14:12,220 --> 05:14:14,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Stricto po ang requirement.

4494
05:14:14,300 --> 05:14:22,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magiging instructor one ka lang with plantilla item kung ikaw ay merong MA or MS.

4495
05:14:23,360 --> 05:14:23,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

4496
05:14:25,200 --> 05:14:33,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Subalit, sa SUCs, ang merong MA or MS na instructor one, salary grade 12 lang po.

4497
05:14:34,240 --> 05:14:35,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Salary grade 12.

4498
05:14:36,320 --> 05:14:36,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

4499
05:14:37,400 --> 05:14:39,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Samantala, sa ibang mga ahensya ng gubernator,

4500
05:14:39,120 --> 05:14:40,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa ibang mga ahensya ng gobyerno, notably sa DEPED,

4501
05:14:41,340 --> 05:14:44,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: guidance counselor, MA requirement, salary grade 16.

4502
05:14:45,540 --> 05:14:50,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Master teacher one, MA requirement, salary grade 18.

4503
05:14:50,380 --> 05:14:53,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam ko sa UP, nakikita ko si Chancellor Vistan eh.

4504
05:14:54,020 --> 05:14:57,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung mga MA holder nila, assistant professor yan.

4505
05:14:58,140 --> 05:14:59,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Salary grade 18, tama.

4506
05:15:00,160 --> 05:15:05,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Salary grade 18, assistant professor ang title pag may MA.

4507
05:15:06,520 --> 05:15:16,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero sa mga ibang SUCs, sa ating 112 other SUCs ay salary grade 12.

4508
05:15:17,360 --> 05:15:25,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So panahon na po para iwas to, itama ang napakatinding injusticia na to.

4509
05:15:25,740 --> 05:15:31,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So bakit, katulad ng nabanggit ko kanina, kung ikaw ay nurse,

4510
05:15:33,120 --> 05:15:42,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: wala kang MA, registered nurse, mag-apply ka sa government hospital, salary grade 15 ka.

4511
05:15:44,020 --> 05:15:49,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero pag mag-apply ka sa SUC, sa College of Nursing, para magturo, kailangan may MA ka.

4512
05:15:50,260 --> 05:15:54,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Meron ka ng MA, tinanggap ka, instructor 1, salary grade 12 ka.

4513
05:15:55,200 --> 05:15:55,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit po?

4514
05:15:55,740 --> 05:16:02,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So maling-mali, panahon na para iwas to, may commitment ang CHED.

4515
05:16:03,860 --> 05:16:11,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil nilatag na po natin ang problema, hinarap na natin sa Kongreso at sa mga ahensya na concerned.

4516
05:16:12,560 --> 05:16:20,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: CHED, Civil Service Commission, DBM at Kongreso, kailangan iwas to na po natin ang injusticia na to.

4517
05:16:20,300 --> 05:16:24,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, nag-commit ang CHED na kagyat.

4518
05:16:25,740 --> 05:16:28,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Harapin nila ang DBM at Civil Service Commission.

4519
05:16:28,860 --> 05:16:34,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So we expect that this will be acted upon soon.

4520
05:16:34,360 --> 05:16:40,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibig po sabihin yan, pag tinaas natin yung instructor 1 to salary grade 16,

4521
05:16:41,280 --> 05:16:46,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: eh dapat po, pati yung ibang mga posisyon, necessarily, kailangan tumaas din.

4522
05:16:46,460 --> 05:16:48,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Na dapat lamang.

4523
05:16:49,180 --> 05:16:55,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil deserve ng mga faculty ang mas mataas na posisyon.

4524
05:16:55,740 --> 05:17:03,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At po, ay biktima ng inyustisyang ito, dapat harapin na natin.

4525
05:17:04,460 --> 05:17:10,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibigay natin sa ating mga faculty ang deserve nila.

4526
05:17:11,200 --> 05:17:17,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pinagtrabahuhan nyo ang inyong professional qualifications, dapat sweldohan kayo ng tama.

4527
05:17:17,440 --> 05:17:23,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, sinusuportan po ba ng sponsor?

4528
05:17:24,080 --> 05:17:24,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang ah...

4529
05:17:25,740 --> 05:17:28,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pagwasto natin sa salary grade ng mga instructor 1?

4530
05:17:29,600 --> 05:17:31,420
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Yes po, ah, Madam Speaker.

4531
05:17:31,720 --> 05:17:37,220
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ah, kasama nyo po kami sa pagsusulong po ng pagpapataas po ng kanilang salary grade.

4532
05:17:37,400 --> 05:17:43,500
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: At, ah, bilang pong anak ng isang teacher, ah, ako rin po ay, ah, ano po, sangayon po sa inyong pinapanukala.

4533
05:17:43,500 --> 05:17:45,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Maraming salamat po, Madam Speaker.

4534
05:17:46,160 --> 05:17:48,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hanggang doon na lamang po ang aking interpellation.

4535
05:17:49,340 --> 05:17:49,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, thank you.

4536
05:17:55,740 --> 05:17:57,280
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Majority Leader.

4537
05:17:57,820 --> 05:18:04,840
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Madam Speaker, I move that you recognize the Honorable Reneco, I mean, Sara Elago, for her interpellation.

4538
05:18:05,020 --> 05:18:11,920
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Sara Elago of, ah, Gabriela Partilis is hereby recognized for her interpellation. Please proceed.

4539
05:18:15,920 --> 05:18:18,220
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat, Madam Speaker.

