Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: may ongoing, sa mga ongoing, ngayong September pa lamang,

5800
06:24:07,340 --> 06:24:15,600
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: inire-release na po nila kanilang mga scholarship, kanilang pondo sa mga scholars para po sa mga ongoing na programs.

5801
06:24:15,600 --> 06:24:21,100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I hope, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, na itong mga ganito ma-realize po natin.

5802
06:24:21,200 --> 06:24:26,140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Hindi po ito matali para sa mga batang pumapasok, lalo na kung madi-delay yung allowance nila ng ganyan.

5803
06:24:26,640 --> 06:24:36,840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Meron naman po sigurong miscellaneous fund ang mga SUCs na baka pwedeng pagkuna ng allowance nila pag nadidelay yung pagbayad natin.

5804
06:24:41,740 --> 06:24:42,760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Pusible po ba yun?

5805
06:24:43,980 --> 06:24:44,880
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ano po kasi?

5806
06:24:44,880 --> 06:24:49,280
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ang pondo po na nga para sa ating doktor pa sa bayan ay mula po sa MSIRES Fund.

5807
06:24:49,800 --> 06:24:55,980
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ito po ay nakalaan lang po specifically para po mapondohan ang scholarship na ating mga estudyante.

5808
06:24:56,660 --> 06:25:03,600
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: At mula po sa CHEDAD sa PASOK, yun lamang po ang kanilang paraan para mapondohan po itong mga…

5809
06:25:03,600 --> 06:25:12,860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What I'm asking, Distinguished Colleague, Mr. Speaker, is that if this happens again, we have a solution na pwede nilang pagkunan.

5810
06:25:13,500 --> 06:25:14,860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, ano po?

5811
06:25:14,880 --> 06:25:24,260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ano po ang pwedeng ipropose ng SUCs para po hindi ito maulit-ulit na kahit magkaroon ng delay, which is improbable na hindi magkakaroon ng delay,

5812
06:25:25,360 --> 06:25:28,240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ang huwag naman po mag-antay ay yung mga bata.

5813
06:25:44,880 --> 06:25:51,180
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ang binigay po ng solusyon, ang pinayop pong solusyon ng CHEDAD at ng PASOK,

5814
06:25:51,320 --> 06:25:54,640
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: ay yung mula po sa umpisa ng semestre,

5815
06:25:55,360 --> 06:26:02,060
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: kailangan na po nilang maybigay ang billing statement para po sa mga scholars.

5816
06:26:02,480 --> 06:26:08,820
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ayun po yung magiging udyok po para mas mabilis po yung processing ng pag-release ng scholarship funds.

5817
06:26:08,820 --> 06:26:12,820
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: At sila naman po ay nangako na yun po ay magiging…

5818
06:26:14,880 --> 06:26:22,060
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: magiging best practice po para sa lahat ng mga SUCs para po may patuloy na po yung early billing para po sa ating mga estudyante.

5819
06:26:22,660 --> 06:26:32,520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Speaker, sa mga nakapagtapos at nakapasa na sa licensure exam, ilan ang nagsasagawa na ng return service?

5820
06:26:33,940 --> 06:26:41,840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Particularly in communities lacking government physicians, may we request the figures and funding gaps per participating SUC?

5821
06:27:14,880 --> 06:27:25,000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Distinguished sponsor, in the interest of time, pwede bang isubmit na lang?

5822
06:27:26,440 --> 06:27:40,820
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Yes, distinguished colleague. They have given a current figure of 615 number of graduates po sa status ng scholars but they will be able to provide you with further data on the issue po.

5823
06:27:40,820 --> 06:27:58,480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you. Mr. Speaker, hinihiling ko na sa 1.5 billion na proposed allocation para sa bagong Pilipinas Merit Scholarship ay unahing kunin ang pondong kailangan para sa scholarships ng qualified solo parents at kanilang mga anak.

5824
06:27:58,480 --> 06:28:09,540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: At para sa doktor, para sa bayan, may mga batas na po tayong ipinasah para sa kanila ngunit hindi pagganap na napupondohan.

5825
06:28:09,540 --> 06:28:13,000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Sana, unahin po natin ito pa rin yung mga ito.

5826
06:28:14,400 --> 06:28:19,880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Maari namang isama ang mga qualified beneficiaries na ito sa bagong Pilipinas Scholarships.

5827
06:28:20,480 --> 06:28:29,900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Dala pa rin ito ang pangalan at prioridad ng ating Pangulo habang tinutugunan ang mga obligasyong itinakda na ng Congress.

5828
06:28:30,760 --> 06:28:34,060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Sana po ay maisaayos natin ito sa budget amendments process.

5829
06:28:35,060 --> 06:28:39,520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kung hindi ito maaaring gawin at kailangan manatiling hiwalay ang bagong Pilipinas,

5830
06:28:39,540 --> 06:28:53,740
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Pilipinas Merit Scholarship, hinihikayat ko ang DBM na pondohan po additionally mula sa available uncommitted HEDF balance.

5831
06:28:55,060 --> 06:29:03,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Alinsunod sa batas upang ang 1.5 billion sa proposed budget ay ma-prioridad para sa solo parents law at doktor para sa bayan.

5832
06:29:03,860 --> 06:29:09,220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Speaker, may I urge our distinguished sponsor to help us pursue this.

5833
06:29:09,540 --> 06:29:12,460
Rep. Roberto Nazal: With the Committee on Appropriations and DBM,

5834
06:29:13,400 --> 06:29:15,880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: supportado natin ang priority program ng Pangulo,

5835
06:29:16,100 --> 06:29:22,800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ngunit kailangan din natin matugunan ang mga batas na ipinasan natin para sa ating solo parents at future doctors.

5836
06:29:24,020 --> 06:29:30,620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ang sinasabi ko lang naman po, both programs are pinasa po natin under namang batas.

5837
06:29:31,220 --> 06:29:37,560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Pero parang anang nangyayari na prioritize natin yung bagong Pilipinas Merit Scholarship.

5838
06:29:37,640 --> 06:29:39,100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Baka naman pwedeng kunin din po.

5839
06:29:39,540 --> 06:29:45,640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: My next question, Mr. Speaker, distinguished colleagues.

5840
06:29:45,640 --> 06:30:00,020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mayroon po bang unpaid deficiencies from earlier academic years at bagong kakulangan para sa year 2025-2026 at 2026-2027?

5841
06:30:00,000 --> 06:30:08,160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: May we request a breakdown by SUC and academic year including the funding source and payment schedule?

5842
06:30:11,900 --> 06:30:24,780
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Towards the new schooling, Mr. Speaker, CHED will be happy to provide the detailed breakdown of per SUCs covered by the deficiency.

5843
06:30:24,780 --> 06:30:37,560
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: But in general, there's a deficiency of 2.048 billion for the year of 2026 in terms of free higher education funding.

5844
06:30:38,100 --> 06:30:48,700
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: And for the year 2027, the incoming year, there will be a deficiency of 2.76 billion pesos to the total of 5.321 billion pesos.

5845
06:30:49,280 --> 06:30:52,340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: How do we expect to cover that?

5846
06:30:52,340 --> 06:30:54,700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Paano po natin sa mga habol yung deficiency?

5847
06:30:54,780 --> 06:31:08,640
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Ang binigay po na solusyon ng CHED, una po would be to increase the tuition of our students and to cover for the deficiency from DBM.

5848
06:31:09,620 --> 06:31:21,860
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: May meron po ngayong inaaral na formula kung ano po yung pinakamainam na pagtaas para sa ating mga estudyante na para hindi naman po masaktan ang kanilang financial status.

5849
06:31:23,200 --> 06:31:24,740
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Sa ngayon po, yun po ang...

5850
06:31:24,780 --> 06:31:30,580
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Pinopost po ng CHED para po masolusyonan po yung deficiency na iyan.

5851
06:31:31,640 --> 06:31:38,200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor, may I ask, anong student services yung mga naapektuhan?

5852
06:31:39,400 --> 06:31:47,280
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And may we request DBM to explain whether legally available savings could have augmented the deficient appropriate items?

5853
06:31:50,180 --> 06:31:54,760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Sapat na ba ang proposed 2027 funding upang hindi na maulit ang saan?

5854
06:31:54,780 --> 06:32:15,640
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Sa ngayon po, wala pa po tayong kasama DBM dito pero rest assured po to our distinguished colleague that we'll be able to furnish you an explanation po from DBM regarding the query po kung ano po yung maaaring nilang magiging proposed source ng funding po para makover po yung deficiency na iyan.

5855
06:32:15,640 --> 06:32:22,420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I was suggesting, Distinguished Colleague, natanongin ng SUCs sa DBM.

5856
06:32:22,900 --> 06:32:24,640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kung pwedeng yung legally...

5857
06:32:24,780 --> 06:32:38,900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: My next question, Mr. Speaker, ilang academic buildings sa ating SUCs ang hindi pa natatapos?

5858
06:32:39,620 --> 06:32:45,320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Magkano na ang nagastos at magkano pa ang kailangan upang magamit ang mga to?

5859
06:32:47,280 --> 06:32:51,700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kulang ba ang pondo o may implementation delays ba at sino po ang accountable?

5860
06:32:54,780 --> 06:33:15,780
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: Mr. Speaker, sa ngayon po, mula po sa ulat po ng ating pasok, lahat po ng mga state universities and colleges kaya na may ongoing na infrastructure projects.

5861
06:33:15,780 --> 06:33:22,180
Rep. Karl Fernandez Legazpi: At lahat po yun ay napondohan mula sa gaon natin sa 2026.

5862
06:33:22,900 --> 06:33:23,780
