Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, sa ilalim ng Republic Act No. 12316, binigyan ng Pangulo ng kapangyarihang magsuspinde o magbawas ng excise tax sa petroleum products kapag ang average ng Dubai crude oil price ay umabot o lumagpas na sa $80

8303
08:05:40,000 --> 08:06:09,980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: kada bariles. Ang rekomendasyon ay manggagaling sa DBCC in coordination sa DOE. Maaari po ba nating malaman kung ano ba ang naging rekomendasyon ng DOE sa DBCC? Lalong-lalo na po ngayon sunod-sunod ang oil price hikes. Noong September 22 lamang nagpatupad na naman ng panibagong malaking oil price hike.

8304
08:06:09,980 --> 08:06:39,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kada litro sa diesel nasa 6.47, sa kerosene 4.88, sa gasolina [unclear]. Ayon mismo sa DOE, ito na ang ikatlong sunod na malaking oil price increase ngayong Setyembre. Kung pagsasamahin po natin ang tatlong magkakasunod na oil price hikes ngayong buwan, umabot na sa [unclear] sa diesel lamang, nasa 16.67 sa kerosene at 15.25 sa gasolina.

8305
08:06:39,980 --> 08:06:53,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa ngayon, umaabot na sa nasa 104 kada litro ang presyo ng diesel at 87 kada litro naman sa gasolina. Ano po ang rekomendasyon ng DOE hinggil dito?

8306
08:06:53,320 --> 08:07:09,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Just to clarify, Mr. Speaker, ang trabaho po ng DOE ay only to submit the certification sa DBCC na nag-over na po tayo sa $80 per barrel. But it is up to the DBCC to act on it.

8307
08:07:09,980 --> 08:07:15,000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Wala na po sa kapangyarihan ng DOE.

8308
08:07:15,000 --> 08:07:39,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, malinaw po naabot o lumagpas na doon sa trigger na presyo. May certification na rin mula sa DOE. Ang kinakailangan na lang po ay agarang aksyon sa pagpapababa sana po ng presyo ng petroleum products. At kahapon lamang naglabas ng anunsyo ang DOF na sususpendihin po ang excise

8309
08:07:39,980 --> 08:08:15,190
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: taxes sa LPG at kerosene. Naniniwala po ba ang DOE na nararapat din na maisama na ang pagsuspende ng excise tax sa diesel at gasolina? Lalong-lalo na po ngayong araw nagsimula na rin ang strike ng ating mga jeepney drivers at iba pang public utility drivers. Nananawagan na rin ang mga provincial at city bus drivers, operators at kanilang mga kumpanya na dapat mas malawak na aksyon para pababain ang presyo ng langis sa ating bansa.

8310
08:08:15,200 --> 08:08:36,000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes. As much as we want to answer, Mr. Speaker, wala na po kasi sa mandato ng DOE. It's up to the economic managers to decide. Mahirap pong sumaklaw sa kapangyarihan na hindi nakapaloob sa Department of Energy.

8311
08:08:36,000 --> 08:08:39,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, good sponsor, kailangan po sanang busisiin natin yung naipasa nating batas.

8312
08:08:39,980 --> 08:09:09,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kasi po nanggaling din dito ang Department of Agriculture at ang posisyon po nila, hindi nga lang pagsususpende, pagbabawas ng excise taxes sa petroleum products. Ang panawagan nila, maski po yung 12% value-added tax sa petroleum products, lalong-lalo na po sa crudo na ginagamit ng maraming mangingisda at magsasaka, ay dapat meron nang aksyon.

8313
08:09:09,980 --> 08:09:39,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nandiyan din ang mga nabanggit kong jeepney drivers, operators, companies na nananawagan ng dagliang aksyon. Ang sinasabi po sa atin, hindi lang ng DOE kundi ng iba pang departamento, DOF ang dapat kalampagin pagdating sa agarang rekomendasyon para sa aksyon ng Malacañang.

8314
08:09:39,980 --> 08:10:09,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Napakalayo po ng DOF doon sa mga pinakaapektadong sektor ng pagtaas ng presyo ng langis: drivers, manggagawa, magsasaka at mangingisda. Nababahala tayo na baka maulit ang nakita natin noong unang kwarto ng taon, kung saan LPG at kerosene lang ang agarang aksyon pero hindi ang parehong urgency para sa diesel at gasolina.

8315
08:10:09,980 --> 08:10:37,000
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nais ko ring magtanong sa DOE: meron po ba tayong inaasahang dagdag-singil sa susunod na linggo o buwan? Ano ang prospects ng presyo ng langis? Nakikita po ba natin ang pagbaba o pagtaas at paano po tayo naghahanda dito?

8316
08:10:37,000 --> 08:10:39,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Well, that depends on the international market.

8317
08:10:39,980 --> 08:10:51,000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Wala po tayong control diyan. Pag tumaas sa international market, sigurado pong tataas. Pag bumaba, sigurado rin pong [unclear].

8318
08:10:51,000 --> 08:11:09,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Muli, Ginoong Speaker, ginoong sponsor, dito sa kapulungan na ito kasalukuyan na rin tayong nag-aaral ng mga amyenda sa kaugnay na batas para matiyak na hindi tayo nakaasa lamang sa ini-import na langis.

8319
08:11:09,980 --> 08:11:39,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dito mismo sa ating bansa, palakasin ang kakayahan na mag-supply sa kinakailangang sektor at industriya. Muli, pinapanawagan natin, at nanggaling din kanina ang Office of the President, gamitin ang emergency powers para suspendihin o bawasan ang excise tax sa petroleum products.

8320
08:11:39,980 --> 08:12:09,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dito sa Kongresong ito, busisiin na tanggalin ang excise taxes sa petroleum products at aralin ang pagbabasura sa value-added tax sa langis. Ngayon naman po tungkol sa trabaho ng National Electrification Administration. Habang pinoproblema ang mataas na singil sa kuryente, may halos tatlong milyong Filipino households pa ang wala pa ring access sa kuryente.

8321
08:12:09,980 --> 08:12:32,720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kung halos tatlong milyon ang unserved households, bakit milyon-milyong kabahayan pa rin ang walang kuryente? Maaari bang ibahagi ang profile ng natitirang unserved households at ilan ang nasa geographically isolated and disadvantaged areas?

8322
08:12:32,720 --> 08:12:39,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, regarding that, we can submit detailed data to the distinguished colleague.

8323
08:12:39,980 --> 08:13:09,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang population po natin ay hindi kumokonti kundi lumalaki, at may budgetary constraints. That's why NEA is asking for additional funding para sa sitio electrification. Nag-aaral din ang NEA dahil ang sitios ay lumalaki at humahaba.

8324
08:13:09,980 --> 08:13:35,400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: When you put a sitio electrification program in one community na minimum ten houses, pag may kuryente na, lalayo na naman yung tao at papakuryentehan mo na naman sila. We have to review the electrification limitations, kasi kung hindi, baka buong kabundukan natin may linya na ng kuryente.

8325
08:13:35,400 --> 08:13:39,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor,

8326
08:13:39,980 --> 08:14:09,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sa plano po ba ng DOE, kailan natin maaabot ang pinakamalapit sa 100% electrification? Naintindihan ko pong malaking issue ang pagkuha ng datos sa PSA; kung tama ang pagkakatanda ko, 2018 pa ang datos na ginagamit. Ang pinakahuling datos na makakatulong sa pagpopondo at pagpaplano ay hindi pa natin nakikita.

8327
08:14:09,980 --> 08:14:30,000
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sinabi ninyong kailangan ng mas malaking pondo at suporta, pero may malaking challenges pa sa pag-abot ng 100%. Ano sa ngayon ang ating mga plano?

8328
08:14:30,000 --> 08:14:39,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: This may not be accurate, Mr. Speaker, kasi lumalaki ang population. But based on the population now, kung ito ang ating kokuryentehan,

8329
08:14:39,980 --> 08:14:48,040
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: we need 67 billion and it will be done by 2033.

8330
08:14:48,040 --> 08:15:00,398
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, ang access sa reliable at abot kaya na kuryente napakahalaga sa pag-aaral, sa edukasyon, sa kabuhayan, sa kalusugan, sa komunikasyon ng bawat pamilyang Pilipino.

8331
08:15:00,398 --> 08:15:11,400
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kailangan maabot ang mga communities na nananatiling underserved at unserved, lalong-lalo na sa mga malalayong lugar na matagal nang naghihintay ng access sa servisyo na ito.

8332
08:15:11,800 --> 08:15:15,700
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dapat po natin tiyakin na ang kuryente ay abot kaya maasaan at tuloy-tuloy.

8333
08:15:15,900 --> 08:15:23,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya po, dito rin sa Kongreso, bubusisiin po natin marami pong mga panukala ngayon na may kinalaman tungkol dyan.

8334
08:15:24,040 --> 08:15:28,300
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman tungkol sa gasoline station training and loan funds.

8335
08:15:28,300 --> 08:15:42,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ayon sa COA, may 81.3 million pesos na accumulated amount sa ilalim ng gasoline station training and loan fund o GSTLF as of December 31, 2024.

8336
08:15:42,600 --> 08:15:46,220
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ito ay bahagi ng 300 million fund na manggagaling sa PAGPOR.

8337
08:15:47,240 --> 08:15:50,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ito po ay ayon sa Republic Act No. 8479.

8338
08:15:50,340 --> 08:15:57,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At ayon din sa COA, 14 years na ang nakalipas pero hindi pa rin nagagamit o underutilized.

8339
08:15:57,340 --> 08:16:03,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ang pondong ito dahil walang gustong mag-loan sa hirap ng mga rekesitos nito.

8340
08:16:04,100 --> 08:16:10,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kasama sa recommendations ng COA na maglabas ang DOE ng Department Circular para amyendahan ng guidelines,

8341
08:16:11,420 --> 08:16:13,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: kaugnay ng application dito.

8342
08:16:13,840 --> 08:16:16,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: 2024 pa ang recommendation na ito.

8343
08:16:16,060 --> 08:16:26,900
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron na po bang nagawa ang DOE tungkol sa pagre-review ng guidelines sa paggamit ng pondo na ito?

8344
08:16:27,340 --> 08:16:35,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker. As of now kasi wala pong nag-apply but the DOE will amplify.

8345
08:16:36,300 --> 08:16:44,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Siguro po mas malaman po na ating mga taong bayan na meron ganitong programa para po mag-apply po sila.

8346
08:16:45,960 --> 08:16:51,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, malinaw po yung observation tsaka yung recommendation.

8347
08:16:51,060 --> 08:16:57,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hindi lang po ito tungkol sa awareness. Maaaring factor yung awareness, yung kakulangan ng information.

8348
08:16:57,340 --> 08:17:02,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Tungkol sa paggamit at application ng Gasoline Station Training and Loan Funds.

8349
08:17:03,000 --> 08:17:09,780
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pero ang sinabi po dito sa particular ay yung hirap ng mga requirements, ng mga rekesitos.

8350
08:17:10,060 --> 08:17:12,980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya maaari ba ang pag-aralan ng DOE?

8351
08:17:13,220 --> 08:17:20,460
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Agad, huwag na po tayo makintay hanggang sa susunod pa na taon para ma-review ang guidelines tungkol sa application nito.

8352
08:17:20,460 --> 08:17:27,240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, Mr. Speaker, nais ko lang din po na maidagdag na ang layunin naman,

8353
08:17:27,340 --> 08:17:38,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: nitong GSTLF ayon sa oil deregulation law ay ma-promote at ma-encourage ang active at direct participation ng private sector at cooperatives

8354
08:17:38,960 --> 08:17:49,740
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sa retailing ng petroleum products sa pamamagitan ng mga joint venture supply agreements sa mga industry participants para po sa establishment ng gasoline stations.

8355
08:17:49,740 --> 08:17:55,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pero sa kasalukuyan na kalagayan na ilang mga major oil players lamang ang nandyan,

8356
08:17:56,540 --> 08:17:57,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: halos wala po.

8357
08:17:57,340 --> 08:18:04,160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Siguro talagang mangangahas na dumaan dun sa napakahirap na proseso para lang mangutang sa GSTLF.

8358
08:18:04,500 --> 08:18:11,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nakuha na po natin yung commitment ng ating sponsor, ng departamento, at aabangan po natin yan.

8359
08:18:12,400 --> 08:18:22,580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dahil hindi lang po ito tungkol sa pag-review mismo ng guidelines ng circular, pero tungkol din ito sa pagsasabansa mismo ng industriya ng lanis

8360
08:18:22,580 --> 08:18:26,780
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para gawin sanang sentralisado ang procurement ng mga produktong petrolyo,

8361
08:18:27,340 --> 08:18:35,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: may iwasan ang price manipulation para sa mas mabilis at direkta na pagbibigay ng subsidyo sa panahon ngayon ng krisis.

8362
08:18:36,200 --> 08:18:50,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman po tungkol sa proposed oil storage facility ng Abu Dhabi National Oil Company at Saudi Aramco para sa itatayong commercial facility dito sa Pilipinas.

8363
08:18:50,340 --> 08:18:57,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maari po bang mag-update sa atin ang ating distinguished sponsor kung ano po ang status ng planong storage facility?

8364
08:18:57,340 --> 08:19:01,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Na ito ng ADNOC at Saudi Aramco.

8365
08:19:02,460 --> 08:19:08,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, 50 million barrels ang target nila, 500 hectares po ang kailangan para dito.

8366
08:19:09,880 --> 08:19:14,560
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At abate po sa balita sa Zamboanga po ang nakikitang lupa na pwedeng pagtayuan.

8367
08:19:15,220 --> 08:19:18,560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, it's Zamboanga and even Bataan, Mr. Speaker.

8368
08:19:19,080 --> 08:19:26,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And as of now, nag-uusap na po with PNOC regarding this matter.

8369
08:19:26,260 --> 08:19:29,180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, nandito pa rin po tayo sa pag-aaral.

8370
08:19:30,580 --> 08:19:44,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, wala pa pong definite na since nag-aaral pa lang po tayo, so hindi po natin pwedeng sagutin ng mas accurate or mas defined yung inyong katanungan.

8371
08:19:44,780 --> 08:19:48,540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But on process na po yung pag-uusap with PNOC.

8372
08:19:49,040 --> 08:19:55,180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, nag-uusap pa lang po ang DOE at ang mga nabanggit ng mga kumpanya.

8373
08:19:56,260 --> 08:19:57,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Come again, Mr. Speaker.

8374
08:19:59,480 --> 08:20:01,680
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pinag-aaralan pa lang po ng DOE ang proposals?

8375
08:20:01,960 --> 08:20:03,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang PNOC po.

8376
08:20:03,840 --> 08:20:04,620
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ng PNOC?

8377
08:20:04,700 --> 08:20:04,960
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

8378
08:20:05,180 --> 08:20:06,180
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang mga proposals mula?

8379
08:20:06,280 --> 08:20:06,540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

8380
08:20:06,760 --> 08:20:06,980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Okay.

8381
08:20:07,660 --> 08:20:07,900
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Alright.

8382
08:20:08,160 --> 08:20:10,580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At may kasama pa po ba tayo, ibang agencies?

8383
08:20:11,140 --> 08:20:13,900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But yung commitment po is by 2028.

8384
08:20:14,700 --> 08:20:15,080
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: By 2028?

8385
08:20:15,080 --> 08:20:17,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: One million barrels po.

8386
08:20:17,640 --> 08:20:18,100
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Okay, so.

8387
08:20:18,300 --> 08:20:20,880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung for storage, Mr. Speaker.

8388
08:20:21,180 --> 08:20:22,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: One million lamang po?

8389
08:20:22,440 --> 08:20:22,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

8390
08:20:22,720 --> 08:20:23,120
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Okay.

8391
08:20:23,640 --> 08:20:25,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nakita po kasi natin sa balita ang target.

8392
08:20:25,880 --> 08:20:26,800
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At nasa 50 million.

8393
08:20:27,080 --> 08:20:29,660
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So, pinabalita niyo po ngayon nasa one million lang.

8394
08:20:30,340 --> 08:20:31,140
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So, for both locations.

8395
08:20:31,140 --> 08:20:33,380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: po for 2028. That's the target

8396
08:20:33,620 --> 08:20:33,660
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Okay.

8397
08:20:33,660 --> 08:20:34,140
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: 2028.

8398
08:20:34,720 --> 08:20:34,980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Alright.

8399
08:20:35,180 --> 08:20:35,500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Sige po.

8400
08:20:35,760 --> 08:20:42,760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Bukod po ba sa PNOC, meron pa po ba tayong ibang mga kausap na agencies ng ating pamahalaan

8401
08:20:42,760 --> 08:20:43,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: kapag dating dito?

8402
08:20:44,000 --> 08:20:48,160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Halimbawa po, natanong ko ito kasi sa pag-identify natin ng location.

8403
08:20:49,060 --> 08:20:52,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Halimbawa, kung meron pong mga nakatira doon

8404
08:20:52,760 --> 08:20:55,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: o kaya naman ay ginagamit para sa agensya.

8405
08:20:55,880 --> 08:20:57,180
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Agrikultura, halimbawa.

8406
08:20:57,700 --> 08:21:01,500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Meron na po ba sa ngayon na coordination with other agencies

8407
08:21:01,500 --> 08:21:03,640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: pagdating sa paggamit ng lupa?

8408
08:21:04,320 --> 08:21:08,360
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: As of now, wala pa naman pong defined talaga kung saan po mismo.

8409
08:21:08,580 --> 08:21:09,400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We know the area.

8410
08:21:09,940 --> 08:21:14,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But yung specific location, hindi pa po yun na pa-finalize.

8411
08:21:14,880 --> 08:21:20,120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But definitely, PNOC po kasi iba naman po yung mandato po nila.

8412
08:21:20,120 --> 08:21:25,120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But they have to coordinate siguro po with DAR, with DNR, other government agencies.

8413
08:21:25,880 --> 08:21:31,200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But we have to assure na hindi po mawawalan ng bahay

8414
08:21:31,200 --> 08:21:39,200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: o ang ating pong mga constituents na pwedeng apektoan ng pagtatayang po ng ating planta.

8415
08:21:39,860 --> 08:21:41,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat, ginoong speaker.

8416
08:21:42,440 --> 08:21:44,660
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At patuloy naman natin na susubay ba yan?

8417
08:21:44,660 --> 08:21:50,840
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Diba ng ating kapulungan, ang pagtitiyak, halimbawa, na sangayon sa ating mga batas,

8418
08:21:50,960 --> 08:21:54,640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na sangayon sa mga existing po natin ng mga palisya,

8419
08:21:54,640 --> 08:21:59,700
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: hinggil sa proteksyon, halimbawa, sa agrikultura, sa kalikasan,

8420
08:22:00,080 --> 08:22:03,360
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ang kung anuman na itatayo ng mga bagong storage facility.

8421
08:22:03,900 --> 08:22:09,960
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman po, yung nabanggit nyo po kanina na Bataan,

8422
08:22:10,420 --> 08:22:16,100
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ito po ba yung 15 million barrel reserve sites sa Bataan?

8423
08:22:16,100 --> 08:22:17,100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 15 million?

8424
08:22:18,120 --> 08:22:18,820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sa Bataan?

8425
08:22:23,320 --> 08:22:23,920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually,

8426
08:22:24,640 --> 08:22:28,140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Speaker, doon po tayo mag-uumpisa ng project.

8427
08:22:28,380 --> 08:22:34,080
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, regarding yung specific na 15 million?

8428
08:22:34,340 --> 08:22:36,760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Yes, 15 million barrel reserve.

8429
08:22:36,780 --> 08:22:40,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Well, hindi po sa Bataan lang yan, it can be spread all over the country.

8430
08:22:42,140 --> 08:22:44,800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, not specifically 15 million po for Bataan.

8431
08:22:45,760 --> 08:22:50,580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Okay, sa ngayon po ba meron na kayong pag-aaral o maaring maibahagi sa kapulungan na ito at sa publiko

8432
08:22:50,580 --> 08:22:54,580
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na kung matutuloy ang particular na proyekto na ito ng PNOC?

8433
08:22:54,640 --> 08:23:02,020
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kasi, ay ilang araw, linggo o buwan ang itatagal ng oil reserve na mailalagak sa site na yan.

8434
08:23:05,220 --> 08:23:10,520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: One million barrels, it's only about two to three days, Mr. Speaker.

8435
08:23:11,520 --> 08:23:16,160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Mr. Speaker, a distinguished sponsor, yan po ang dahilan kung bakit sa tinpo natin,

8436
08:23:16,240 --> 08:23:23,020
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: bagamat marami po tayong mga pagsisikap para matiyak na may mga dagdag tayo na facilities para sa storage,

8437
08:23:23,020 --> 08:23:23,840
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para po.

8438
08:23:23,840 --> 08:23:27,740
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Patiyak na magkakaroon tayo ng oil reserve, hindi po asapat.

8439
08:23:28,220 --> 08:23:38,440
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kinakailangan pa rin na pag-aaralan po natin paano ba magkakaroon ng mas matibay at matatag na centralized procurement system.

8440
08:23:39,020 --> 08:23:44,000
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At yung pag-aaral natin dito sa Kongreso tungkol sa pagsasabansa ng industriya ng lanis.

8441
08:23:44,540 --> 08:23:53,020
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Patagal na po sinusulong ng Gabriela Women's Party kasama po ang mga partylist sa ilalim po ng makabayan koalasyon.

8442
08:23:53,840 --> 08:23:58,920
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ang House Bill No. 8125 o ang Downstream Oil Industry Regulation Act.

8443
08:23:59,180 --> 08:24:04,300
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nandiyan din po ang House Bill No. 8126, ang Centralized Petroleum Procurement Act.

8444
08:24:04,620 --> 08:24:08,820
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nandiyan din po ang bill tungkol din sa renationalization ng Petron.

8445
08:24:08,920 --> 08:24:16,760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: So yan lang po yung ilan dun sa mga panukala na amienda kasabay din nung unbundling ng oil prices.

8446
08:24:16,760 --> 08:24:23,760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Isa pa po yan, yung pagtitiyak din ng transparency sa mga singil at pagpapababa ng singil sa landas.

8447
08:24:23,840 --> 08:24:26,700
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Langis ganun din po sa kuryente.

8448
08:24:26,860 --> 08:24:33,040
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya po, sana ang mga panukalang batas na ito ay agaran na matalakay dito sa Kongreso

8449
08:24:33,040 --> 08:24:38,500
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: upang maiwasan po natin ang malakartel na gawi ng mga malalaking players

8450
08:24:38,500 --> 08:24:43,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na madalas po ay lubos-lubos ang pagkita mula sa ordinaryong mamamayan

8451
08:24:43,880 --> 08:24:52,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: habang nakikita po natin na yung kita nila ay lubos na paghihirap sa ordinaryong mamamayan Pilipino.

8452
08:24:52,340 --> 08:24:53,280
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya muli.

8453
08:24:53,840 --> 08:24:58,840
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Naway, mapalakas po natin ang industriyalang langis para sa mga ordinaryong Pilipino.

8454
08:24:59,200 --> 08:25:02,060
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming maraming salamat, Ginong Speaker, Mr. Sponsor.

8455
08:25:02,180 --> 08:25:03,200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

8456
08:25:04,020 --> 08:25:07,040
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Thank you, Honorable Ilago, Majority Leader.

8457
08:25:07,660 --> 08:25:12,780
Rep. Ryan S. Recto: Mr. Speaker, I move to recognize the Honorable Tino from the ACT Teachers Party List to interpolate the sponsor.

8458
08:25:13,460 --> 08:25:18,480
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: The Honorable Antonio Tino of ACT Party List is recognized. Please proceed.

8459
08:25:22,740 --> 08:25:23,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maganda.

8460
08:25:23,840 --> 08:25:27,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magandang hapon. Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

8461
08:25:28,320 --> 08:25:29,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilang mga katanungan.

8462
08:25:30,880 --> 08:25:39,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, una, yung kasalukuyang energy emergency.

8463
08:25:40,100 --> 08:25:40,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Di ba?

8464
08:25:41,180 --> 08:25:53,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of course, alam natin, unang nadeklara ito earlier in the year dahil sa gera ng USA-Iran beginning of March onwards.

8465
08:25:53,840 --> 08:26:00,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tapos, tumaas ang presyo ng gasolina at diesel, LPG, lahat na.

8466
08:26:01,060 --> 08:26:08,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon, at the height of that crisis, bumili po ng diesel, direct procurement ng diesel at LPG,

8467
08:26:10,140 --> 08:26:16,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang, well, Department of Energy, ang gobyerno ng Pilipinas.

8468
08:26:16,320 --> 08:26:23,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ayon sa mga datos na binigay sa atin, bumili po ng 21,000 liters,

8469
08:26:23,840 --> 08:26:26,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: of LPG, okay?

8470
08:26:26,800 --> 08:26:36,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And also, diesel and gasoline amounting to 268,180,012 liters.

8471
08:26:39,100 --> 08:26:42,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kakamustahin po natin kung ano na ang status ng mga ito.

8472
08:26:44,080 --> 08:26:50,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ayon po sa inyong datos, yung 21,000 liters of LPG

8473
08:26:50,560 --> 08:26:53,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay,

8474
08:26:53,840 --> 08:26:57,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: alos, mahigit, kumulang kalahati po nito ay,

8475
08:26:57,920 --> 08:27:03,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay wala na or committed na.

8476
08:27:03,900 --> 08:27:08,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Either, well, iklaro natin, binenta ba?

8477
08:27:09,000 --> 08:27:09,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Or na-commit?

8478
08:27:10,380 --> 08:27:11,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At kanino, if ever?

8479
08:27:12,680 --> 08:27:16,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: But, according to your data, of the 21,000 liters,

8480
08:27:16,440 --> 08:27:20,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: now only 11,100,

8481
08:27:20,760 --> 08:27:23,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 11.15,000,

8482
08:27:23,840 --> 08:27:29,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 11,000 liters na lamang ang nasa storage as of August 2026.

8483
08:27:30,060 --> 08:27:31,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ano po nangyari dun sa,

8484
08:27:32,600 --> 08:27:36,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: more or less, half of the purchased LPG?

8485
08:27:38,860 --> 08:27:43,020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Regarding the LPG, yung 21,000 na binagay niyo po, ay nabenta na.

8486
08:27:43,520 --> 08:27:46,620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: At karamihan po ang bumili is mga LPG players.

8487
08:27:47,340 --> 08:27:48,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: LPG players.

8488
08:27:48,420 --> 08:27:51,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ano po ang nangyari dito?

8489
08:27:51,400 --> 08:27:51,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So,

8490
08:27:51,520 --> 08:27:52,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: um,

8491
08:27:52,240 --> 08:27:54,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kumita ba?

8492
08:27:54,440 --> 08:27:55,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nalugi ba?

8493
08:27:55,400 --> 08:27:55,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Or,

8494
08:27:56,480 --> 08:27:59,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: nakatulong ba sa pag-maintain,

8495
08:28:00,080 --> 08:28:02,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pag-stabilize o pagbaba ng presyo ng LPG?

8496
08:28:03,460 --> 08:28:04,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil dito?

8497
08:28:06,960 --> 08:28:08,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How much was it sold for?

8498
08:28:09,520 --> 08:28:10,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually po,

8499
08:28:10,360 --> 08:28:11,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: lugi po tayo sa...

8500
08:28:11,700 --> 08:28:12,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Lugi po.

8501
08:28:12,380 --> 08:28:16,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O pwede pong ipaliwanag kung paano ang nangyari?

8502
08:28:17,320 --> 08:28:18,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We bought it at,

8503
08:28:18,340 --> 08:28:18,620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: ah,

8504
08:28:26,120 --> 08:28:29,350
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: You bought it by—

8505
08:28:29,360 --> 08:28:30,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: You bought it about 70,

8506
08:28:31,820 --> 08:28:34,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and you sold it at 53.

8507
08:28:35,140 --> 08:28:35,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: At 50,

8508
08:28:36,020 --> 08:28:36,980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: bought at 70,

8509
08:28:37,640 --> 08:28:39,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: and sold at 53 per liter.

8510
08:28:40,360 --> 08:28:40,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes.

8511
08:28:40,660 --> 08:28:42,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: To commercial providers.

8512
08:28:42,380 --> 08:28:42,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Tama po.

8513
08:28:43,080 --> 08:28:43,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes.

8514
08:28:43,780 --> 08:28:44,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah,

8515
08:28:44,120 --> 08:28:44,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: presumably,

8516
08:28:45,760 --> 08:28:47,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: anong naging epekto nito?

8517
08:28:48,060 --> 08:28:49,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nagresulta pa ito sa

8518
08:28:49,520 --> 08:28:51,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pagbaba ng presyo

8519
08:28:51,440 --> 08:28:52,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: o pag-maintain ng presyo?

8520
08:28:53,220 --> 08:28:55,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ang masasabing efekto nito

8521
08:28:55,220 --> 08:28:55,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa merkado?

8522
08:28:55,480 --> 08:28:57,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, it stabilized the supply,

8523
08:28:57,840 --> 08:28:58,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Speaker.

8524
08:28:58,380 --> 08:29:00,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, so in an effort to stabilize,

8525
08:29:01,580 --> 08:29:02,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay ginawa po yun.

8526
08:29:03,140 --> 08:29:04,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon, meron pa pong natitira

8527
08:29:04,640 --> 08:29:08,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 11,100 plus liters.

8528
08:29:08,860 --> 08:29:09,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that correct?

8529
08:29:09,540 --> 08:29:10,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This is as of August.

8530
08:29:11,340 --> 08:29:12,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May natitira pa po?

8531
08:29:14,140 --> 08:29:15,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Wala na po, Mr. Speaker.

8532
08:29:15,300 --> 08:29:17,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: As of August, ito po yung report nyo.

8533
08:29:17,100 --> 08:29:19,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: As of August, it's only middle of September.

8534
08:29:19,740 --> 08:29:21,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, wala na po ba?

8535
08:29:21,980 --> 08:29:22,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Wala na po.

8536
08:29:22,840 --> 08:29:23,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, in other words,

8537
08:29:23,700 --> 08:29:27,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: you sold off another 11,000 liters?

8538
08:29:28,320 --> 08:29:28,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, itong August.

8539
08:29:28,720 --> 08:29:28,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8540
08:29:29,940 --> 08:29:30,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alright.

8541
08:29:33,360 --> 08:29:35,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How about the diesel and gasoline purchases?

8542
08:29:35,920 --> 08:29:38,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, high-profile po itong mga purchases na ito.

8543
08:29:38,540 --> 08:29:41,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Some of them, if I'm not mistaken,

8544
08:29:41,140 --> 08:29:43,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: were direct purchases from Russia.

8545
08:29:46,300 --> 08:29:49,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, umabot daw sa

8546
08:29:49,740 --> 08:29:52,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 200 liters na lang gagamitin natin

8547
08:29:52,080 --> 08:29:52,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: para standard,

8548
08:29:53,680 --> 08:29:56,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 268,000,

8549
08:29:56,380 --> 08:29:58,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: more than 268,000 liters

8550
08:29:58,640 --> 08:30:00,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang binili.

8551
08:30:00,000 --> 08:30:08,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ayon sa datos na sinubmit nyo, tapos ngayon, 181.7 thousand liters in storage.

8552
08:30:09,460 --> 08:30:10,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Still in storage.

8553
08:30:11,160 --> 08:30:15,060
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Correct, Mr. Speaker, but I would like to clarify, wala po tayong binili sa Russia.

8554
08:30:15,700 --> 08:30:18,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, okay. Wala pong binili sa Russia.

8555
08:30:18,460 --> 08:30:18,900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8556
08:30:18,900 --> 08:30:25,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Thank you for that clarification. So, saan po binili? More or less, ah...

8557
08:30:26,200 --> 08:30:27,140
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Traders, ah...

8558
08:30:27,140 --> 08:30:27,500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Traders.

8559
08:30:27,500 --> 08:30:28,020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Mr. Speaker.

8560
08:30:28,020 --> 08:30:29,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Through Singapore. Parang ganun po.

8561
08:30:30,760 --> 08:30:31,640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8562
08:30:31,800 --> 08:30:34,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sige, walang binili sa Russia. Okay.

8563
08:30:36,860 --> 08:30:44,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, may 181.7 thousand liters still in storage as of your submission, August.

8564
08:30:45,400 --> 08:30:47,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ganun pa rin po ba? This is still in storage?

8565
08:30:47,360 --> 08:30:48,460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, you are correct, Mr. Speaker.

8566
08:30:48,780 --> 08:30:50,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Of the...

8567
08:30:50,880 --> 08:30:51,940
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: More or less, Mr. Speaker.

8568
08:30:52,060 --> 08:30:57,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: More or less. And this is diesel and gasoline. Tama po?

8569
08:30:57,100 --> 08:30:58,160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8570
08:30:58,360 --> 08:30:58,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8571
08:30:58,600 --> 08:31:12,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Ngayon, tinatanong po natin, anong nangyari doon sa more or less 80... roughly 80 thousand liters. What happened to that?

8572
08:31:12,960 --> 08:31:27,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Meron po kayong report that 6.4 million liters were sold to PNOCEC for off-grid SPAG power generation at a preferential...

8573
08:31:28,600 --> 08:31:30,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ...preferential rate of 80 pesos per liter.

8574
08:31:30,960 --> 08:31:31,460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

8575
08:31:31,460 --> 08:31:32,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po?

8576
08:31:32,160 --> 08:31:33,840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: You are absolutely correct.

8577
08:31:33,840 --> 08:31:52,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes. Yan po yung datos na sinabit nyo. So, in other words, nakabili kayo ng diesel. At that time, mataas pa yung presyo nun. That was over a hundred. Tapos, binenta nyo at a preferential rate. So, mas mura. 80 pesos per liter para dun sa missionary areas na gumagamit ng diesel generators.

8578
08:31:52,660 --> 08:31:53,160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

8579
08:31:53,160 --> 08:31:57,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, presumably, nakatulong sa pagpapababa o pag-maintain.

8580
08:31:58,360 --> 08:32:03,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nung mas mababang presyo ng kuryente. Okay. Ano po nangyari doon sa iba pa?

8581
08:32:04,660 --> 08:32:08,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It was sold to the traders, Mr. Speaker.

8582
08:32:08,340 --> 08:32:18,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No, kasi 6.4 million lamang yung binenta sa PNOCEC for off-grid.

8583
08:32:19,460 --> 08:32:27,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, meron pang natitira po na more than 80 thousand liters na...

8584
08:32:28,360 --> 08:32:30,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Unaccounted for in your report.

8585
08:32:31,800 --> 08:32:38,800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes. Binenta rin po yan sa mga oil companies. Especially yung mga nakikigamit po tayo ng mga facilities po nila.

8586
08:32:39,440 --> 08:32:44,220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Kasi wala po tayong facility. So, dun po napunta yung pagbenta po.

8587
08:32:44,300 --> 08:32:50,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, binenta sa oil companies at a preferential rate of 80 pesos per liter? Is that it?

8588
08:32:50,640 --> 08:32:51,100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: No. No.

8589
08:32:51,100 --> 08:32:54,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No. At o, yun po. Pwedeng magpaliwanag po.

8590
08:32:54,240 --> 08:32:58,100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, there's a formula. Yung pagbenta based on...

8591
08:32:58,360 --> 08:33:02,800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Singapore MOPs price, Mr. Speaker.

8592
08:33:02,800 --> 08:33:06,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, so based on the prevailing MOPs price.

8593
08:33:07,040 --> 08:33:09,400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes. Magkaiba po yung treatment.

8594
08:33:09,600 --> 08:33:09,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8595
08:33:10,140 --> 08:33:12,980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung sa NAPOCOR and sa oil companies, magkaiba po yan.

8596
08:33:13,200 --> 08:33:24,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, mula nung pumasok po ito in several shipments, ay binibenta nyo na po sa private companies. Ganun po ba?

8597
08:33:25,840 --> 08:33:28,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Not necessarily, Mr. Speaker.

8598
08:33:28,360 --> 08:33:29,640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: It took a while also.

8599
08:33:29,780 --> 08:33:44,100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, what is... Pwedeng paki-explain. What was the policy? How is this... How did the DOE dispose of this... At least a portion of this purchase, direct purchase by government?

8600
08:33:44,760 --> 08:33:45,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Anong patakaran?

8601
08:33:45,660 --> 08:33:52,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Naintindihan natin. Sige, pagbenta tayo sa PNOCEC para sa missionary electrification.

8602
08:33:52,300 --> 08:33:52,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What do you mean?

8603
08:33:52,760 --> 08:33:55,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero, paano po yung sa private companies? What is the policy there?

8604
08:33:55,880 --> 08:33:59,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sir, first, ah, Mr. Speaker, may supply po tayo. Okay?

8605
08:33:59,360 --> 08:33:59,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8606
08:33:59,620 --> 08:34:04,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Regarding the policy on pagbenta po sa private, we follow the Singapore MOPs price.

8607
08:34:05,580 --> 08:34:06,020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay.

8608
08:34:06,580 --> 08:34:14,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hindi po kasi pwedeng specific kasi iba-iba po yung nangyayari. Like, every week, every day, nag-iba po yan. World market, nag-iba yan.

8609
08:34:14,540 --> 08:34:22,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, ang ginawa lang po talaga ng ating government is to make sure na may supply po tayo ng diesel.

8610
08:34:22,800 --> 08:34:25,860
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Lalo na kung wala tayong supply ng diesel, mas problema po.

8611
08:34:25,880 --> 08:34:26,880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Para sa ating bayan.

8612
08:34:27,040 --> 08:34:39,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero, para po, paano po nakatiyak ang gobyerno at ang DOE na yung binenta sa private ay nag-translate sa mas mababang presyo?

8613
08:34:39,980 --> 08:34:49,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Baka mamaya, pinatungan din nila, di lugi ang taong bayan, ang taxpayer at ang consumer.

8614
08:34:49,480 --> 08:34:55,400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes. Actually, Mr. Speaker, ang pagbenta po ng DOE o ng PNOC.

8615
08:34:55,880 --> 08:35:01,820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Sa ating mga oil players, depende pa rin sa market price. So, yun din po yung sinusunod natin.

8616
08:35:02,800 --> 08:35:08,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, market price. So, hindi necessarily naka-resulta sa pagbaba ng presyo.

8617
08:35:08,980 --> 08:35:09,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

8618
08:35:09,380 --> 08:35:09,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8619
08:35:09,980 --> 08:35:20,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, hindi po ba pwede? Bakit hindi po ginawa? Alam ko pinag-uusapan nyo noon, bakit hindi ginawa na direct ang ibenta ng DOE at a lower rate yung diesel?

8620
08:35:21,340 --> 08:35:25,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And you still have 181,000.

8621
08:35:25,880 --> 08:35:29,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 181,000 liters in storage, as reported.

8622
08:35:29,080 --> 08:35:40,280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We truly understand that, Mr. Speaker. But there are also restrictions within DOE, lalo na po sa COA. So, wala po sa mandato ng DOE na magbenta po ng…

8623
08:35:40,280 --> 08:35:55,180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, sinasabi nyo po, nakatali ang kamay ng DOE, hindi pwede yung direct… some arrangement where this diesel and gasoline may be sold at a preferential rate, at a lower rate.

8624
08:35:55,180 --> 08:36:05,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: To the consumers. So, yung po sinasabi nyo. Or, di kaya, through the… yung fuel subsidy program, hindi po ba pwede yun?

8625
08:36:06,440 --> 08:36:11,100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, fuel subsidy, we can do it. But it's not really the DOE's doing it.

8626
08:36:11,540 --> 08:36:11,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8627
08:36:12,420 --> 08:36:13,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Implementing it, Mr. Speaker.

8628
08:36:13,980 --> 08:36:14,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ano po ang plano?

8629
08:36:15,060 --> 08:36:17,320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The DOTr po yung nag-implement po noon.

8630
08:36:17,320 --> 08:36:23,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ang plano ng DOE sa 181 million liters in storage?

8631
08:36:25,180 --> 08:36:31,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diesel and gasoline. Ganun din lang po. Benta pa rin sa pribadong sektor.

8632
08:36:32,220 --> 08:36:37,360
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes. Yung 181, we have to dispose it in a calibrated way, Mr. Speaker.

8633
08:36:37,800 --> 08:36:42,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have to be very prudent. We have to study it. Hindi po basta ang ididispose mo.

8634
08:36:42,340 --> 08:36:48,460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We have to study also the situation, not only in the Philippines, but the world market.

8635
08:36:49,080 --> 08:36:54,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Pero ang masiguro lang po natin na hindi po maubusan ng supply ng diesel ang Pilipinas.

8636
08:36:54,440 --> 08:36:55,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, for sure.

8637
08:36:55,180 --> 08:37:03,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May lugi na po dyan. Dahil ito, binili ito, nasa mga 120, 150 pesos per liter ang diesel at the time.

8638
08:37:04,340 --> 08:37:14,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: E ngayon, hindi pa naman. Umaabot. Pero hindi pa lumalag pa sa, I think, 100 pesos per liter ang diesel.

8639
08:37:15,240 --> 08:37:18,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, definitely, kung ibenta mo ngayon ito, definitely may lugi.

8640
08:37:18,720 --> 08:37:25,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya nga po, dapat maingat na we don't, hindi natin gustong i-subsidize yung tubo ng,

8641
08:37:25,180 --> 08:37:30,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng, ah, gobyerno or malugi ang gobyerno unnecessarily. Diba?

8642
08:37:30,540 --> 08:37:33,020
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, you are absolutely correct, Mr. Speaker.

8643
08:37:33,040 --> 08:37:36,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Anyway, so, binabantayan po natin ang mangyayari dito.

8644
08:37:37,740 --> 08:37:53,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, ngayon, since we're on the topic, ah, ano po, I mean, at ayon sa mga, ah, analyst, ay mukhang tatagal pa yung crisis sa supply

8645
08:37:53,380 --> 08:37:55,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng, ah, fuel.

8646
08:37:55,180 --> 08:38:00,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: With, ah, still the problem in the Strait of Hormuz. Diba?

8647
08:38:01,040 --> 08:38:01,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

8648
08:38:01,800 --> 08:38:11,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, tumataas na naman muli ang presyo, lalo na, specifically of diesel, not just because of the supply, but issues with refining capacity globally.

8649
08:38:12,060 --> 08:38:25,170
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No? Ah, it's also the war in Iraq, ah, sorry, the war in Ukraine. Diba? The Ukraine war, ah, which has resulted in destruction of, ah, refining capacity.

8650
08:38:25,180 --> 08:38:37,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In, ah, Russia, among others. Yung Iran war naman, ah, may epekto sa refining capacity, obviously, in the Gulf states. And Iran itself. Okay?

8651
08:38:38,400 --> 08:38:51,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, so, mukhang tatagal pa to. Ah, ano po ang kakayahan ngayon ng, ah, DOE at ng gobyerno para magpatuloy sa mga, ah, safety net or mitigating measures?

8652
08:38:51,900 --> 08:38:54,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May sapat na pondo pa po ba?

8653
08:38:55,180 --> 08:39:05,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang DOE, ah, o ang administrasyon in general, alam ko bahagi naman ng DOE sa pagpaplano dyan, ah, para matugunan.

8654
08:39:05,640 --> 08:39:15,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Paano kung pumalo muli tayo sa more than 100 pesos per, per liter na diesel na hindi malayong mangyari yan? No? In the near future.

8655
08:39:15,440 --> 08:39:25,000
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I agree, Mr. Speaker, but, ah, ang DOE po is policymaking body, but at the end of the day, executive decision po yan. What we can do is make recommendations.

8656
08:39:25,180 --> 08:39:33,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We can make studies. Ah, we can recommend to the DBCC, but at the end of the day, ah, economic managers po ang mag-de-decide.

8657
08:39:34,220 --> 08:39:50,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Now, as to the storage, so, meron kayong, ah, 181.7 liters in storage in several facilities. Ah, tama po ba isa sa mga pinakamalaking facilities for storage is the one in Subic? Is that correct?

8658
08:39:50,760 --> 08:39:51,780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8659
08:39:51,780 --> 08:39:54,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Oo. At, ah, yung...

8660
08:39:55,180 --> 08:40:06,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung facility na yun sa Subic is that the Philippine Coastal Storage, ah, facility in Subic. That is the single largest fuel storage facility in the country, correct?

8661
08:40:07,380 --> 08:40:08,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8662
08:40:08,720 --> 08:40:13,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ginagamit po ba ito ng DOE para sa kanilang, ayun, yung binanggit natin?

8663
08:40:14,120 --> 08:40:15,220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8664
08:40:15,220 --> 08:40:19,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How much of the 181 million liters is there?

8665
08:40:25,180 --> 08:40:33,440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ah, in barrels, we have, ah, about 900, 8,000 to 900,000 barrels, ah, Mr. Speaker.

8666
08:40:34,520 --> 08:40:35,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, in there?

8667
08:40:35,900 --> 08:40:36,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8668
08:40:36,860 --> 08:40:46,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, hindi lang yung, ah, yung, yung purchase kung hindi more than that? Parang ganun po ba? Okay. Ah...

8669
08:40:46,020 --> 08:40:48,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Um, barrels po, ah, Mr. Speaker.

8670
08:40:48,940 --> 08:40:49,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Barrels.

8671
08:40:50,320 --> 08:40:51,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Barrels. Barrels.

8672
08:40:51,780 --> 08:40:52,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 159 liters per barrel.

8673
08:40:52,700 --> 08:40:54,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 159 liters per barrel.

8674
08:40:55,020 --> 08:40:55,040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8675
08:40:55,040 --> 08:40:55,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, if you compute it...

8676
08:40:55,520 --> 08:40:58,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, 159 million liters. Is that correct?

8677
08:40:59,020 --> 08:41:03,680
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: No, 159 per barrel. So, compute ka nga. More or less, Mr. Speaker.

8678
08:41:03,680 --> 08:41:06,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, barrel. Barrel. Oh, you're using barrels. Oh, I get it. Okay.

8679
08:41:06,900 --> 08:41:07,280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, barrels, yeah.

8680
08:41:07,420 --> 08:41:13,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O, sige po. Anyway, so ginagamit. Pero ang isang issue po dito, of course, this is privately owned.

8681
08:41:13,520 --> 08:41:24,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And currently, the majority owner of that is, in fact, the U.S. investment firm, I-Squared.

8682
08:41:25,040 --> 08:41:25,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba?

8683
08:41:26,620 --> 08:41:27,780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8684
08:41:27,780 --> 08:41:41,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Wala po ba kayong nakikitang issues that a significant part of the country's, ah, very limited strategic reserve is, ah, in a facility actually owned by a foreign corporation?

8685
08:41:42,120 --> 08:41:48,380
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Well, as of now, ah, we have no choice. That's why ang recommendation po ng DOE is magtayo po ng sarili.

8686
08:41:48,640 --> 08:41:49,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8687
08:41:49,120 --> 08:41:50,800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Because, ah, we are also paying rent.

8688
08:41:51,360 --> 08:41:54,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And is it not also true that the, ah, that facility...

8689
08:41:54,880 --> 08:42:07,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The Philippine Coastal Storage Facility in Stubic, ah, also, ah, holds, ah, the Navy, ah, the fuel reserves of the U.S. Navy?

8690
08:42:08,780 --> 08:42:21,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No? Ah, kaya po pagka dumadaong dyan yung mga barko ng U.S. Navy, ah, they refuel from there in the tanks of the Philippine Coastal Storage.

8691
08:42:21,400 --> 08:42:22,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po ba ganun din?

8692
08:42:23,180 --> 08:42:24,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang issue po dito is...

8693
08:42:24,880 --> 08:42:44,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po ba magiging vulnerable ang ating significant, ah, although meager, strategic reserves, ah, since they are stored, ah, collocated, no, in the same facilities as U.S. Navy facilities?

8694
08:42:44,360 --> 08:42:54,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam po natin yung nangyari. Pinakita na ng gera sa Iran. Target po yan. No, ganun na nangyari. Tinarget yung mga fuel depo sa Bahrain.

8695
08:42:54,880 --> 08:43:08,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa Kuwait, sa UAE, at iba pa. Hindi po ba pinag-iisipan to ng Department of Energy? In other words, security. The security of our energy reserves. Paano po yun?

8696
08:43:08,680 --> 08:43:20,880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Actually, ah, Mr. Speaker, um, yung information po, number one, di po alam ng DOE. Ah, thank you for informing us regarding yung sa military, et cetera.

8697
08:43:20,880 --> 08:43:21,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Okay. Ah, po.

8698
08:43:21,720 --> 08:43:24,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But, um, hindi po natin hiningi yung gera ng...

8699
08:43:24,720 --> 08:43:53,540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: American Iran. And, ah, naghanap po tayo ng secured na pening paglagyan ng reserve po natin. And dun po natin nakita po sa Subic. That's why we did it. So, because we have no choice. Wala po tayong sariling depo. That's why, ah, we were forced to good na gamitin po yun. Pwede mas malaki po ang problema ng ekonomiya pag napabayaan po natin at wala po tayong diesel sa ating bansa.

8700
08:43:54,720 --> 08:44:09,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, okay. So, anyway, ah, apparently, hindi alam ng DOE. Pero yun po ang realidad, no? So, hopefully, mapag-iisipan ng DOE yung usapin din ng seguridad ng ating energy reserves, no?

8701
08:44:09,080 --> 08:44:24,080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Especially since the current foreign policy of the Marcos Jr. Administration is to expand the military footprint of the U.S. in using our critical civilian infrastructure.

8702
08:44:24,720 --> 08:44:54,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Including the fuel storage facilities in Subic. So, anyway, let me move on. Ah, dahil limitadong oras, yun naman po usapin ng issues related to the grid. Ah, yung mga yellow and red alerts. Binigyan din po tayo ng datos ng DOE. At, ah, parang may summary po ng mga red and yellow alerts.

8703
08:44:54,720 --> 08:44:59,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In Luzon and Visayas and Mindanao grids, no? So...

8704
08:45:00,000 --> 08:45:25,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, this is from January to the present at pinakamapalad po ang Luzon grid dahil, well, ayon dito ay there have been a total of four yellow alerts and three red alerts for the Luzon grid.

8705
08:45:25,640 --> 08:45:48,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, total seven. Pero sa Visayas grid po, sa Visayas grid, from beginning of the year to September, okay, at least first week of September, yung datos dito, there have been a total of 92 days of yellow alert and 29 of red alert.

8706
08:45:50,260 --> 08:45:54,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And sa Mindanao grid naman, ay...

8707
08:45:55,640 --> 08:45:57,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Apektado na rin.

8708
08:45:58,220 --> 08:46:04,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa Mindanao grid, a total of ten yellow alerts and four red alerts.

8709
08:46:05,320 --> 08:46:11,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pagka yellow and red alert, ibig po sabihin yan, brown out. Tama po ba?

8710
08:46:11,160 --> 08:46:20,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. At ako, personal na naranasan ko po, ibig sabihin pinakamalala po sa Visayas at nagpapatuloy pa po. Tama po ba?

8711
08:46:21,780 --> 08:46:22,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes, Mrs. Speaker.

8712
08:46:22,420 --> 08:46:25,160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes. Ako mismo, naranasan ko dahil nga...

8713
08:46:25,640 --> 08:46:34,800
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Nakailang beses akong pumunta sa Visayas, particular sa Visayas, sa Cebu City at saka sa Bacolod.

8714
08:46:35,620 --> 08:46:40,360
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: At doon talaga, sabi nila, well, ganito talaga yan. Yung Bacolod, dalawang beses.

8715
08:46:41,480 --> 08:46:46,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi nila talaga, araw-araw, merong rotating, at least one hour a day.

8716
08:46:47,240 --> 08:46:51,060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: On that particular day I was there, 12 hours po yung outage.

8717
08:46:52,620 --> 08:46:55,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa Cebu naman, nagmi-meeting kami.

8718
08:46:55,640 --> 08:47:00,680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mga bandang ala 5, ala 6, in the middle of the meeting, nawala na ang kuryente.

8719
08:47:02,060 --> 08:47:03,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, yun talaga, ganun.

8720
08:47:03,620 --> 08:47:09,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ako talaga, tas naririnig ko, nagsa-start up ng mga generator para magkakuryente.

8721
08:47:09,800 --> 08:47:20,480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, na-deja vu po ako, nung mga kabataan natin, 1990s, na araw-araw, merong mga power outage.

8722
08:47:20,620 --> 08:47:24,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tapos yung mga may kaya, meron silang generator.

8723
08:47:24,600 --> 08:47:25,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba?

8724
08:47:26,400 --> 08:47:26,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8725
08:47:27,520 --> 08:47:28,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, bakit po ganyan?

8726
08:47:29,080 --> 08:47:33,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang pangako ng IPIRA, sabi nila, una, bababa ang presyo ng kuryente.

8727
08:47:33,980 --> 08:47:37,240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam natin, di totoo yun. Di bumaba. Tumaas pa nga.

8728
08:47:37,920 --> 08:47:45,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pangalawang pangako, sabi, because of IPIRA, because of deregulation, masosolve yung problema ng supply.

8729
08:47:46,720 --> 08:47:46,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

8730
08:47:47,700 --> 08:47:50,220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And yet, ano nangyari?

8731
08:47:50,220 --> 08:47:51,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang nyari, asa ng pangako?

8732
08:47:52,520 --> 08:47:53,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang bisayas.

8733
08:47:53,300 --> 08:47:57,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit po ganyan? Parang nabalik tayo sa 1990s.

8734
08:47:58,800 --> 08:47:59,740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What's happening?

8735
08:48:00,360 --> 08:48:03,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of course, outages of plants. Tama po ba?

8736
08:48:04,680 --> 08:48:05,500
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8737
08:48:05,640 --> 08:48:05,820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8738
08:48:06,720 --> 08:48:08,600
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So, if I, you want me to reply?

8739
08:48:08,680 --> 08:48:09,000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sige po.

8740
08:48:09,360 --> 08:48:09,620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

8741
08:48:10,420 --> 08:48:16,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Number one, addressing the yellow and red alerts, may ginawa pong action plan ang DOE.

8742
08:48:16,760 --> 08:48:21,460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Number one, investigate and audit power plants with declaring force outages.

8743
08:48:21,980 --> 08:48:22,900
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Outages deployed.

8744
08:48:22,900 --> 08:48:24,560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: By DOE field offices on the ground.

8745
08:48:25,400 --> 08:48:30,260
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Number two, restore forced outrage plants on schedule.

8746
08:48:30,800 --> 08:48:43,440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: CEDC completed September 15, PEDC, October 3, GNPK, September 20, TSI Unit 1, September 19, TSI Unit 2, September 8.

8747
08:48:43,440 --> 08:48:52,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And we also deployed 253 megawatts of battery storage across Cebu, Panay, Leyte, and Negros within.

8748
08:48:53,080 --> 08:48:53,640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 2026

8749
08:48:53,640 --> 08:48:55,480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: To buffer supply gaps.

8750
08:48:56,340 --> 08:49:09,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We also compelled NGCP to execute all outstanding ancillary services contracts, including battery capacity under the August 13 show cost order.

8751
08:49:09,700 --> 08:49:20,740
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: And we also completed assessment of bisayas transmission constraints, including the latest summer corridor to identify near-term fixes.

8752
08:49:21,780 --> 08:49:22,880
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: We also

8753
08:49:22,880 --> 08:49:31,280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: maintain continuous real-time monitoring of generation and transmission conditions to catch problems before they trigger alerts.

8754
08:49:32,080 --> 08:49:38,100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Deploy interim measures, such as power barge and generator sets, where it is needed.

8755
08:49:38,600 --> 08:49:45,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Now, to give you a report, Mr. Speaker, yung ating pong mga planta na nag-breakdown.

8756
08:49:47,420 --> 08:49:51,440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: In the bisayas, I'll talk about the units.

8757
08:49:52,880 --> 08:49:57,200
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thermo-Bisayas Inc. Unit 1, 169 megawatts.

8758
08:49:58,180 --> 08:50:00,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung assessment po to be determined pa.

8759
08:50:01,220 --> 08:50:09,220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But Thermo-Bisayas Inc. Unit 2, by September 2026, online na po sila.

8760
08:50:10,540 --> 08:50:16,220
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Panay Energy Development Corporation Unit, 115 megawatts.

8761
08:50:17,080 --> 08:50:21,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: By 27 October 2026, operational na po sila.

8762
08:50:21,420 --> 08:50:26,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Cebu Energy Development Corporation, 82 megawatts.

8763
08:50:28,300 --> 08:50:32,440
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: By September 5, mag-online na po sila.

8764
08:50:32,860 --> 08:50:39,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Nag-online na po sila last September 4, 2026 at 133700.

8765
08:50:40,840 --> 08:50:42,820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 30 oras, alam po natin.

8766
08:50:43,460 --> 08:50:47,620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Panay Energy Development Corporation Unit 2, 83 megawatts.

8767
08:50:47,620 --> 08:50:50,620
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Online last 21 September 2026.

8768
08:50:51,420 --> 08:50:56,160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: At 307 ng hapon.

8769
08:50:58,720 --> 08:51:02,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: KEPCO, Salcon Power Corporation, this is in the Bisayas still.

8770
08:51:02,960 --> 08:51:07,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Corporation Unit 2, 103 megawatts for assessment.

8771
08:51:08,260 --> 08:51:14,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: But 26 September 2026, oh nagbukas na to.

8772
08:51:15,340 --> 08:51:19,820
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: By 3 o'clock ng hapon, Mr. Speaker.

8773
08:51:19,820 --> 08:51:21,400
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: So this is the report.

8774
08:51:21,420 --> 08:51:22,720
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: This is the report for the Bisayas, Mr. Speaker.

8775
08:51:22,720 --> 08:51:27,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What about the EDC Mahanagdong Geothermal Power Plant Unit 3?

8776
08:51:27,880 --> 08:51:28,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kumusta po?

8777
08:51:31,160 --> 08:51:32,980
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Still under assessment, Mr. Speaker.

8778
08:51:33,060 --> 08:51:36,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Still under assessment, so wala pa po. That's 55 megawatts.

8779
08:51:37,580 --> 08:51:37,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8780
08:51:38,240 --> 08:51:44,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ang sinasabi niyo po na in the last quarter of the year,

8781
08:51:44,560 --> 08:51:50,560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at least, itong sa submission niyo po rito, may 374.

8782
08:51:51,420 --> 08:51:56,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Plus 130 megawatts na posibleng mag-online.

8783
08:51:56,660 --> 08:51:57,200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ganun po ba?

8784
08:51:57,800 --> 08:51:59,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, even more than that, Mr. Speaker.

8785
08:51:59,760 --> 08:52:00,560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Even more than that.

8786
08:52:00,640 --> 08:52:03,360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Actually, mas marami kayo pinasa kesa dun sa sinabit niyo.

8787
08:52:03,740 --> 08:52:10,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ibig po ba sabihin nito, may maasahang relief from the daily rotating brownouts

8788
08:52:10,920 --> 08:52:13,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang mga kababayan natin sa Bisayas.

8789
08:52:13,460 --> 08:52:17,420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam ko pa naman, ang inyong secretary, si Sharon Garin, taga-Iloilo po yan.

8790
08:52:17,420 --> 08:52:21,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ngunit, araw-araw po nagdurusan.

8791
08:52:21,420 --> 08:52:23,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang mga kababayan natin sa Bisayas.

8792
08:52:24,060 --> 08:52:27,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ano po? Mayroon po ba ang relief na maasahan?

8793
08:52:28,420 --> 08:52:30,300
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: With this, Mr. Speaker, I think yes.

8794
08:52:31,120 --> 08:52:31,520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes.

8795
08:52:32,340 --> 08:52:32,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8796
08:52:32,780 --> 08:52:35,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, well, binabantayan po natin dito.

8797
08:52:35,240 --> 08:52:37,600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero, okay, may mga outages.

8798
08:52:38,840 --> 08:52:46,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero, over the longer term, alam po natin, ang pinaka problema rito ay capacity.

8799
08:52:47,040 --> 08:52:48,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: When it is masyado.

8800
08:52:48,020 --> 08:52:51,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya, pag may nag-offline,

8801
08:52:51,420 --> 08:52:54,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: may, ayan na, yellow alert, red alert.

8802
08:52:57,060 --> 08:53:02,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ang ginagawa ng DOE para matiyak na may dagdag na planta.

8803
08:53:03,180 --> 08:53:04,940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun, ultimately, yun po ang kailangan.

8804
08:53:05,980 --> 08:53:07,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At kailan maasahan ito?

8805
08:53:07,780 --> 08:53:09,780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Well, we need new plants, Mr. Speaker.

8806
08:53:09,920 --> 08:53:16,320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: That's why, mas pinapadali po natin, even yung proseso ng pag-apply,

8807
08:53:16,320 --> 08:53:17,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: lalo na mga Genco.

8808
08:53:18,400 --> 08:53:21,320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Nag-ala po tayong mga investors na mag-invest po sa Pilipinas.

8809
08:53:21,420 --> 08:53:36,060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What new capacity is projected to come online at the soonest possible time for the Visayas grid?

8810
08:53:36,340 --> 08:53:37,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And what type of power?

8811
08:53:40,360 --> 08:53:42,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Renewable, non-renewable, etc.

8812
08:53:42,300 --> 08:53:43,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ito na.

8813
08:53:45,300 --> 08:53:48,760
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Total, if I may, yung installed po na capacity.

8814
08:53:51,420 --> 08:53:55,700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi, yung new capacity na lang po na expected or planned.

8815
08:53:55,940 --> 08:53:56,240
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: RE.

8816
08:53:57,340 --> 08:54:01,540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: 500, non-RE is 585 megawatt.

8817
08:54:01,540 --> 08:54:02,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Non-RE po?

8818
08:54:02,520 --> 08:54:02,920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Non-RE.

8819
08:54:03,580 --> 08:54:05,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, by that, you mean coal?

8820
08:54:05,860 --> 08:54:06,580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that coal?

8821
08:54:07,120 --> 08:54:10,920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Coal, oil-based, natural gas, kasama po dyan.

8822
08:54:11,260 --> 08:54:11,540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8823
08:54:13,300 --> 08:54:14,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano-ano po yan?

8824
08:54:14,440 --> 08:54:16,120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pwede po mabigyan tayo ng listahan?

8825
08:54:16,540 --> 08:54:18,100
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, we will submit.

8826
08:54:18,340 --> 08:54:18,780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8827
08:54:19,480 --> 08:54:21,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, in other words, we can expect,

8828
08:54:21,420 --> 08:54:29,380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: over 500 megawatts na non-renewable new power plants in the Visayas.

8829
08:54:29,380 --> 08:54:32,640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, actually, coal LPG and so on.

8830
08:54:33,180 --> 08:54:33,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes.

8831
08:54:33,540 --> 08:54:33,720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po.

8832
08:54:35,040 --> 08:54:35,840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

8833
08:54:35,960 --> 08:54:37,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Listahan na lang po para may detalye.

8834
08:54:38,140 --> 08:54:40,980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Eh, yung sa renewable naman po, meron din po ba?

8835
08:54:41,440 --> 08:54:44,520
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yes, sa renewable, long-term po ito.

8836
08:54:45,040 --> 08:54:48,340
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ang target po natin is 15,101 megawatts.

8837
08:54:48,340 --> 08:54:49,840
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Well, 15,000.

8838
08:54:50,320 --> 08:54:51,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, long-term talaga.

8839
08:54:51,420 --> 08:54:52,560
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yan, long-term talaga.

8840
08:54:52,720 --> 08:54:55,140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At least, we are planning long-term.

8841
08:54:55,280 --> 08:54:58,880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opo, yung binanggit nyo pong non-renewable, anong time frame po yun?

8842
08:54:59,180 --> 08:55:01,480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung non-RE po natin is immediate.

8843
08:55:02,000 --> 08:55:02,320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Immediate?

8844
08:55:02,340 --> 08:55:05,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung total RE po natin na long-term plan.

8845
08:55:06,080 --> 08:55:06,340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

8846
08:55:09,300 --> 08:55:09,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nasaan na yan?

8847
08:55:12,300 --> 08:55:13,700
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Just a minute, Mr. Speaker.

8848
08:55:14,880 --> 08:55:16,540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Data po kasi yung kailangan natin.

8849
08:55:17,340 --> 08:55:18,460
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: I want to be precise.

8850
08:55:21,420 --> 08:55:26,280
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: If I may, Mr. Speaker, can I give you all the list per area?

8851
08:55:27,320 --> 08:55:27,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sige po.

8852
08:55:28,260 --> 08:55:28,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yeah.

8853
08:55:29,200 --> 08:55:29,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon o?

8854
08:55:30,380 --> 08:55:30,920
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Ngayon po.

8855
08:55:31,160 --> 08:55:31,860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Oh, yes, yes.

8856
08:55:31,880 --> 08:55:33,540
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: After magtanong, mag-evolve ko na po sa inyo.

8857
08:55:33,580 --> 08:55:33,900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sige po.

8858
08:55:34,000 --> 08:55:34,840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hingi na lang po natin.

8859
08:55:35,640 --> 08:55:38,300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mr. Speaker, alam kong tapos ng oras.

8860
08:55:38,420 --> 08:55:45,020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero alam ko, ang ating presiding speaker ngayon, taga-Bisayas din po ito.

8861
08:55:45,740 --> 08:55:50,460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At alam ko, nararanasan din niya at ng kanyang mga constituents

8862
08:55:50,460 --> 08:55:51,260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang issue ng...

8863
08:55:51,420 --> 08:55:54,620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Araw-araw na brown-out.

8864
08:55:54,780 --> 08:55:58,640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kaya napaka-importante po na malaman ng mamamayan

8865
08:55:58,640 --> 08:56:04,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kung meron na bang kahit relief,

8866
08:56:04,740 --> 08:56:07,960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: immediate relief sa kanilang araw-araw na kalbaryo.

8867
08:56:08,660 --> 08:56:10,520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya kailangan po natin ang datos na ito.

8868
08:56:10,620 --> 08:56:15,800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At dinidiin natin, pinapakita na naman yung problema sa IPIRA.

8869
08:56:17,300 --> 08:56:20,440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bigo ang pangako na pabababain ang presyo ng kuryente.

8870
08:56:20,540 --> 08:56:21,400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mas mataas pa nga.

8871
08:56:21,420 --> 08:56:25,660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ngayon naman, pati yung adequate supply, hindi rin maibigay.

8872
08:56:25,880 --> 08:56:30,760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kaya tama lang po yung panawagan na ibasura na ang IPIRA

8873
08:56:30,760 --> 08:56:36,920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at hindi nag-work itong framework ng deregulation

8874
08:56:36,920 --> 08:56:45,500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at pag-alis ng direktang kamay ng gobyerno sa industriya ng kuryente.

8875
08:56:46,020 --> 08:56:47,280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat, Mr. Speaker.

8876
08:56:47,540 --> 08:56:49,200
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Thank you, Honorable Tenio.

8877
08:56:49,460 --> 08:56:50,100
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Majority Leader.

8878
08:56:50,100 --> 08:56:51,380
Rep. Daphne A. Lagon: Mr. Speaker.

8879
08:56:51,420 --> 08:56:55,440
Rep. Daphne A. Lagon: I move to recognize Representative Dagooc for his interpellation.

8880
08:56:56,660 --> 08:57:00,260
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Honorable Serio Dagooc of Party Lease APEC is recognized.

8881
08:57:00,500 --> 08:57:01,000
Deputy Speaker Yevgeny Vincente B. Emano: Please proceed.

8882
08:57:04,220 --> 08:57:05,560
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

8883
08:57:05,740 --> 08:57:06,760
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Thank you, Majority Leader.

8884
08:57:08,100 --> 08:57:11,220
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Magandang gabi po sa ating lahat.

8885
08:57:12,100 --> 08:57:16,700
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Lalong-lalo na yung pinakamamahal kong sponsor.

8886
08:57:16,700 --> 08:57:21,140
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: At sa buong pamilya ng Department of Energy,

8887
08:57:22,100 --> 08:57:25,960
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: buti na lang, napakiusapan natin.

8888
08:57:26,040 --> 08:57:27,080
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Madagdagan sana yun.

8889
08:57:28,180 --> 08:57:29,640
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

8890
08:57:29,680 --> 08:57:32,940
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Anyway, I am just listening.

8891
08:57:33,560 --> 08:57:39,120
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: I requested to be the last interpellator because for the interest of time,

8892
08:57:39,980 --> 08:57:44,300
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: I will escape most of the questions.

8893
08:57:44,300 --> 08:57:51,300
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: I will go directly to policy recommendations na pupwedeng i-consider.

8894
08:57:51,420 --> 08:57:56,200
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ang mga pangako-papasok.

8895
08:57:56,460 --> 08:58:00,180
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: I want to thank the leader ng DOE and later on, the ERC.

8896
08:58:01,440 --> 08:58:03,100
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Wala pa si ERC.

8897
08:58:03,100 --> 08:58:09,160
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Now, ang una kong katanungan na distinct sponsor,

8898
08:58:09,160 --> 08:58:13,260
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: ang Department of Energy po ba ay umaamin

8899
08:58:13,260 --> 08:58:17,580
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: na may problema tayo doon sa ating Philippine Energy Plan.

8900
08:58:17,580 --> 08:58:26,160
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Well, we don't see any problem but we are open to suggestion.

8901
08:58:28,280 --> 08:58:32,320
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Actually, whether you will admit it or not, may problema tayo.

8902
08:58:32,420 --> 08:58:38,880
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: The fact na ganito nung nangyari, may problema tayo sa ating Philippine Energy Plan.

8903
08:58:39,540 --> 08:58:42,720
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Hindi realistic yung ginamit natin ng mga data.

8904
08:58:42,720 --> 08:58:52,580
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: That's why last week, I moved for the deferment of the budget of Philippine Statistics Authority

8905
08:58:52,580 --> 08:58:57,160
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: because they failed to provide the latest data.

8906
08:58:57,260 --> 08:59:00,040
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Biroin mo, 2018 pa yung data. Energy to.

8907
08:59:01,240 --> 08:59:04,320
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Hindi tayo makagalaw kung walang energy.

8908
08:59:05,280 --> 08:59:10,180
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So, I think the DOE must admit.

8909
08:59:10,180 --> 08:59:12,700
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kasi kung hindi nyo admit, hindi nyo bagong.

8910
08:59:12,720 --> 08:59:25,120
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Hindi po kasi tayo nagbabase rin sa study ng PSA regarding sa...

8911
08:59:25,120 --> 08:59:30,460
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: No, I only take PSA data as example.

8912
08:59:30,820 --> 08:59:34,200
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Pero sa DOE mismo, ganito na lang.

8913
08:59:36,280 --> 08:59:38,700
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Lahat ng distribution utility,

8914
08:59:38,700 --> 08:59:39,200
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: no?

8915
08:59:41,240 --> 08:59:42,700
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ay yan po.

8916
08:59:42,720 --> 08:59:50,160
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ano po yung pinanggalingan ng lahat ng program sa ating Philippine Energy Plan?

8917
08:59:51,280 --> 08:59:54,420
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: The projections came from the distribution utility.

8918
08:59:54,940 --> 08:59:55,180
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Saan?

8919
08:59:55,420 --> 08:59:59,780
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Power supply procurement plan, distribution development.

8920
09:00:00,000 --> 09:00:11,320
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yung Power Supply Procurement Plan na sinasubmit ay nanggaling po yun sa projection ng mga distribution utility, ano yung mga papasok na load.

8921
09:00:13,060 --> 09:00:27,480
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Pero hindi po in-involve ng Department of Energy ang other government agency na makakatulong that the data being projected by distribution utilities

8922
09:00:27,480 --> 09:00:30,640
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: ay magiging realistic.

8923
09:00:31,360 --> 09:00:37,880
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Puro lang, nakabase tayo sa historical data, last five years, ito yung load growth mo.

8924
09:00:37,880 --> 09:00:44,100
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: O, kung titingnan mo yung halimbawa si Ariel ko, load growth ko 1% lang.

8925
09:00:44,620 --> 09:00:49,840
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Pero biglang may pupunta doon na dalawang malalaking resort, eh wala yun.

8926
09:00:50,400 --> 09:00:52,140
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Outlier, may outlier ka agad.

8927
09:00:52,520 --> 09:00:53,560
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So, recommendation.

8928
09:00:55,340 --> 09:00:56,880
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: The DOE can intervene.

8929
09:00:57,480 --> 09:01:02,720
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ito, a Memorandum of Understanding with the Department of Trade and Industry.

8930
09:01:03,660 --> 09:01:06,640
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kasi doon sa kanila kukuha lahat ng mga ano.

8931
09:01:07,200 --> 09:01:11,060
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: And the Department of Interior and Local Government.

8932
09:01:11,760 --> 09:01:20,540
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: This is based on my experience sa Siargao, biglang nag-overload yung submarine cable kasi hindi ko nahagip yung mga yun.

8933
09:01:21,500 --> 09:01:26,720
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Pupunta na lang sa si Ariel ko, mag-publishing, mag-opening na next week.

8934
09:01:26,720 --> 09:01:27,460
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Eh, sana.

8935
09:01:27,480 --> 09:01:28,120
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Wala ko kukuha.

8936
09:01:28,540 --> 09:01:29,920
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Wala yun sa PSPP ko.

8937
09:01:30,480 --> 09:01:34,360
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Yung infrastructure ko, hindi naman na-aproba ng ERC yun.

8938
09:01:34,740 --> 09:01:38,080
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kung hindi ko ma-justify, bakit lakihan ko yung conductor?

8939
09:01:38,520 --> 09:01:40,060
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Bakit lakihan ko yung substasyon?

8940
09:01:40,320 --> 09:01:41,360
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Dahil wala nga ng load, eh.

8941
09:01:42,100 --> 09:01:44,000
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: So, hindi ko na-edital niya yun.

8942
09:01:44,520 --> 09:01:46,800
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: We need to involve this agency.

8943
09:01:47,460 --> 09:01:50,200
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kasi hawak nila ang mga local government units.

8944
09:01:50,200 --> 09:01:55,540
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Kung pupunta doon, yung mga investor, mag-invest kami.

8945
09:01:56,280 --> 09:01:57,020
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Yung LGO.

8946
09:01:57,480 --> 09:02:00,940
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Must require them to coordinate with the distribution utility.

8947
09:02:01,660 --> 09:02:04,200
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Pag si DTI, may magparegister na business,

8948
09:02:04,920 --> 09:02:09,860
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: require them to coordinate with the distribution utility kung saan sila malukit

8949
09:02:09,860 --> 09:02:12,200
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: para alam ano yung load nila.

8950
09:02:12,460 --> 09:02:15,380
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: They should submit para masama sa ating PSPP,

8951
09:02:15,980 --> 09:02:18,000
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: ba-consider sa ating DDP.

8952
09:02:18,660 --> 09:02:20,480
Rep. Arnie B. Fuentebella: Yeah, we totally agree with the good gentleman.

8953
09:02:20,580 --> 09:02:21,440
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Okay, thank you.

8954
09:02:22,240 --> 09:02:22,620
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Sunod.

8955
09:02:24,220 --> 09:02:26,620
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Marami tayong mga planta.

8956
09:02:26,620 --> 09:02:29,620
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Whether, again, you will admit it or not,

8957
09:02:29,620 --> 09:02:32,440
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: tatlo ang gamit.

8958
09:02:33,500 --> 09:02:39,060
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: 100 mega, yung 80 mega, bilateral contract.

8959
09:02:39,780 --> 09:02:44,260
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Yung 10 mega, pinakontrata ninyo sa ASPA, sa NGCP.

8960
09:02:44,760 --> 09:02:47,820
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Yung 10 mega, bininta nila sa market.

8961
09:02:48,600 --> 09:02:52,700
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: Ngayon, pag nag-force outage yung planta na yan,

8962
09:02:53,420 --> 09:02:56,260
Rep. Sergio C. Dagooc: anong nangyari sa binayaran natin ang ancillary?

8963
09:02:56,620 --> 09:03:00,100
